WEBVTT

1
00:00:31.667 --> 00:00:34.625
<i>I came to Comala
because I was told my father lived here.</i>

2
00:00:35.917 --> 00:00:37.500
<i>One Pedro Páramo.</i>

3
00:00:39.458 --> 00:00:41.000
<i>That's what my mother told me.</i>

4
00:00:43.083 --> 00:00:44.875
<i>And I promised her I'd come,</i>

5
00:00:46.375 --> 00:00:49.542
<i>for she was near death,
and I of a mind to promise her anything.</i>

6
00:00:51.792 --> 00:00:53.333
<i>Before this she had told me,</i>

7
00:00:54.042 --> 00:00:55.958
<i>"Don't ask him for anything."</i>

8
00:00:56.958 --> 00:00:58.917
<i>"Demand of him what's ours."</i>

9
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.208
<i>"For the neglect he showed us, my son…</i>

10
00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:04.792
<i>make him pay."</i>

11
00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:28.708
<i>I never thought I'd keep my promise.</i>

12
00:01:29.542 --> 00:01:31.708
<i>Until I began to fill myself with dreams.</i>

13
00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:35.250
<i>To give flight to illusions…</i>

14
00:01:36.333 --> 00:01:40.708
<i>And I started forming a world built
around the hope that was that man…</i>

15
00:01:41.875 --> 00:01:43.250
<i>my mother's husband.</i>

16
00:02:10.167 --> 00:02:12.583
And why are you headed to Comala,
if I might ask?

17
00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.833
I'm going to see my father.

18
00:02:20.417 --> 00:02:22.458
He'll throw you quite the party.

19
00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:26.250
He'll be glad to see someone.

20
00:02:27.917 --> 00:02:31.250
And what's your father like?

21
00:02:32.333 --> 00:02:33.583
I don't know him.

22
00:02:34.875 --> 00:02:36.833
I just know his name is Pedro Páramo.

23
00:02:41.792 --> 00:02:43.083
You don't say.

24
00:02:46.875 --> 00:02:48.583
Do you know Pedro Páramo?

25
00:02:53.167 --> 00:02:54.167
Who is he?

26
00:02:56.625 --> 00:02:58.167
A living resentment.

27
00:03:08.458 --> 00:03:10.708
- It's hot here.
- Yes.

28
00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:14.375
This is nothing.

29
00:03:15.583 --> 00:03:18.958
You'll feel it worse
when we get to Comala.

30
00:03:19.792 --> 00:03:21.375
They say

31
00:03:22.083 --> 00:03:24.000
many who die there and go to hell,

32
00:03:25.292 --> 00:03:28.125
come back for their blankets.

33
00:03:32.708 --> 00:03:35.167
I'm also Pedro Páramo's son.

34
00:04:00.458 --> 00:04:02.042
You sure we've made it to Comala?

35
00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:03.833
I'm sure, <i>señor.</i>

36
00:04:06.583 --> 00:04:07.958
Why does it look so sad?

37
00:04:09.458 --> 00:04:10.958
It's the times, <i>señor.</i>

38
00:04:18.208 --> 00:04:19.458
It looks abandoned.

39
00:04:20.333 --> 00:04:23.000
It doesn't just look that way. It is.

40
00:04:24.125 --> 00:04:25.625
Nobody lives here.

41
00:04:27.958 --> 00:04:29.083
And Pedro Páramo?

42
00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:33.875
Pedro Páramo died many years ago.

43
00:04:50.417 --> 00:04:52.125
Where can I find a room?

44
00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:56.125
Look for Doña Eduviges
if she's still alive.

45
00:04:56.958 --> 00:04:58.625
Tell her I sent you.

46
00:04:59.417 --> 00:05:00.833
And what's your name?

47
00:05:01.792 --> 00:05:02.792
Abundio…

48
00:05:14.625 --> 00:05:17.958
<i>I bring the same eyes with which
my mother saw these things.</i>

49
00:05:19.083 --> 00:05:20.167
<i>She told me,</i>

50
00:05:20.833 --> 00:05:22.542
<i>"There you'll find my town,"</i>

51
00:05:23.375 --> 00:05:25.042
<i>raised on the hillside,</i>

52
00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:27.917
<i>"full of trees and leaves."</i>

53
00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:31.333
<i>"You'll hear me better there."</i>

54
00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:33.958
<i>"I'll be closer to you."</i>

55
00:05:38.042 --> 00:05:39.875
<i>"I would've liked to tell her,"</i>

56
00:05:41.667 --> 00:05:43.500
<i>"'You lead me astray.'"</i>

57
00:05:44.917 --> 00:05:46.708
<i>"You sent me to a lonesome town."</i>

58
00:05:48.417 --> 00:05:50.333
<i>"Searching for someone who doesn't exist."</i>

59
00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:18.750
Excuse me.

60
00:06:20.083 --> 00:06:22.042
Do you know where Doña Eduviges lives?

61
00:06:23.042 --> 00:06:24.042
Over there.

62
00:06:24.833 --> 00:06:27.458
The pink house with arches.

63
00:06:56.917 --> 00:06:58.500
I'm Eduviges Dyada.

64
00:07:00.417 --> 00:07:01.417
Come in.

65
00:07:12.292 --> 00:07:13.292
This way.

66
00:07:20.167 --> 00:07:21.250
What's all this?

67
00:07:23.083 --> 00:07:24.125
Just stuff.

68
00:07:25.083 --> 00:07:27.667
The house is full of stuff.

69
00:07:29.542 --> 00:07:32.500
Those who left chose it
to store their things,

70
00:07:32.583 --> 00:07:34.667
but nobody has returned for them.

71
00:07:39.083 --> 00:07:40.875
So, you're her son?

72
00:07:42.458 --> 00:07:43.458
Whose son?

73
00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:46.625
Doloritas.

74
00:07:49.333 --> 00:07:50.750
Yes, but how did you know?

75
00:07:51.542 --> 00:07:53.167
She told me you'd be coming.

76
00:07:55.958 --> 00:07:57.375
That you'd come today.

77
00:07:58.542 --> 00:07:59.542
Who? My mother?

78
00:07:59.958 --> 00:08:00.958
Yes.

79
00:08:01.708 --> 00:08:02.708
Her.

80
00:08:08.875 --> 00:08:10.208
This is your room.

81
00:08:13.292 --> 00:08:15.667
I keep it ready in case someone stops by.

82
00:08:21.125 --> 00:08:22.667
There's nowhere to lie down.

83
00:08:24.917 --> 00:08:26.292
Don't worry about that.

84
00:08:27.042 --> 00:08:29.708
Tiredness is a good mattress for fatigue.

85
00:08:31.292 --> 00:08:34.167
It's not easy to arrange
everything in no time.

86
00:08:35.333 --> 00:08:37.792
And your mother didn't
let me know until now.

87
00:08:40.125 --> 00:08:41.333
My mother's dead.

88
00:08:44.333 --> 00:08:46.167
So that's why her voice sounded so weak.

89
00:08:47.542 --> 00:08:48.708
Now I understand.

90
00:08:50.375 --> 00:08:52.042
How long's it been since she passed?

91
00:08:53.708 --> 00:08:55.000
Around seven days now.

92
00:08:56.958 --> 00:08:58.625
She must've felt abandoned.

93
00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.125
We promised we would die together.

94
00:09:02.875 --> 00:09:05.208
To give each other courage
on that final journey.

95
00:09:06.708 --> 00:09:08.583
So, she beat me to it, huh?

96
00:09:10.958 --> 00:09:13.208
But you can be sure I'll catch up to her.

97
00:09:14.875 --> 00:09:16.875
I know how to shorten the paths.

98
00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:20.833
It all consists of dying when one chooses,

99
00:09:21.333 --> 00:09:22.833
and not when He mandates.

100
00:09:25.833 --> 00:09:27.542
First come have a bite to eat.

101
00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:30.833
- A little something.
- I'll come.

102
00:09:34.208 --> 00:09:35.292
I'll come later.

103
00:10:24.542 --> 00:10:26.833
What's taking you so long in the privy,
young man?

104
00:10:27.875 --> 00:10:29.000
Nothing, Mama.

105
00:10:29.667 --> 00:10:33.083
If you stay in there much longer,
a snake will come out and bite you.

106
00:10:35.250 --> 00:10:36.833
Let out more string, Susana!

107
00:10:44.625 --> 00:10:45.667
Good.

108
00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:49.625
- No, no!
- Oh no.

109
00:11:02.250 --> 00:11:03.833
I love this place because of you,

110
00:11:08.167 --> 00:11:10.250
but I hate it for everything else.

111
00:11:12.292 --> 00:11:14.000
Even for having been born here.

112
00:11:22.292 --> 00:11:23.875
I'll come visit from time to time.

113
00:11:26.792 --> 00:11:27.958
You're not coming back.

114
00:11:34.083 --> 00:11:35.208
You'll never return.

115
00:12:46.333 --> 00:12:48.167
I told you to come out of the privy.

116
00:12:49.292 --> 00:12:50.542
I'm coming, Mama.

117
00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:52.833
I'm coming.

118
00:12:52.917 --> 00:12:55.125
Your father says
we can't count on you for anything.

119
00:12:56.833 --> 00:12:58.333
That you're becoming useless.

120
00:13:13.417 --> 00:13:15.500
Shouldn't you be working?

121
00:13:16.333 --> 00:13:17.958
No. Rogelio doesn't pay me.

122
00:13:18.458 --> 00:13:22.917
You don't work at Rogelio's
to earn money. You work there to learn.

123
00:13:24.208 --> 00:13:26.333
For now, you have to resign yourself.

124
00:13:27.667 --> 00:13:29.458
Let others resign themselves, Grandma.

125
00:13:30.625 --> 00:13:32.292
I'm not one for following orders.

126
00:13:33.417 --> 00:13:35.333
You and your strange ideas!

127
00:13:36.542 --> 00:13:39.833
I feel that things won't go well for you,
Pedro Páramo.

128
00:13:44.333 --> 00:13:46.250
<i>I believed that woman was crazy.</i>

129
00:13:48.125 --> 00:13:49.625
<i>Later I didn't believe anything.</i>

130
00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:52.833
<i>I felt in a faraway place</i>

131
00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:55.500
<i>and let myself go.</i>

132
00:13:57.417 --> 00:13:58.458
Yes, it's true.

133
00:13:59.667 --> 00:14:02.000
I was close to being your mother.

134
00:14:05.833 --> 00:14:07.208
She never told you?

135
00:14:09.417 --> 00:14:10.875
She only told me good things.

136
00:14:19.625 --> 00:14:22.292
I heard about you
from the mule driver who brought me here.

137
00:14:23.625 --> 00:14:24.625
A man named Abundio.

138
00:14:25.833 --> 00:14:27.250
He's a good one, that Abundio.

139
00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:31.417
I used to tip him
for each traveler he'd send my way.

140
00:14:32.708 --> 00:14:34.125
Until he went deaf.

141
00:14:36.875 --> 00:14:38.875
The one I'm talking about
could hear just fine.

142
00:14:38.958 --> 00:14:42.042
Anyway, getting back to your mother.

143
00:14:42.917 --> 00:14:45.292
The thing is,
when she was to marry Pedro Páramo,

144
00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:49.792
they told her she could not lie
with a man that night

145
00:14:50.708 --> 00:14:51.958
since the moon was upon her.

146
00:14:54.917 --> 00:14:57.542
So she asked me to go in her place.

147
00:15:03.125 --> 00:15:04.500
You slept with Pedro Páramo?

148
00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:08.708
I got into bed with him gladly.

149
00:15:11.375 --> 00:15:13.708
But the day's excitement

150
00:15:13.792 --> 00:15:16.667
had left him worn out,
and he spent the night snoring.

151
00:15:17.167 --> 00:15:18.833
You were born the following year.

152
00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:21.625
But not to me.

153
00:15:22.125 --> 00:15:23.958
Although it was very close!

154
00:15:27.125 --> 00:15:29.542
Maybe your mother didn't tell you

155
00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:31.750
out of shame.

156
00:15:37.292 --> 00:15:38.917
I brought a portrait of her.

157
00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:45.500
Your mother always loathed Pedro Páramo.

158
00:15:46.875 --> 00:15:50.125
He would do nothing
but complain and order her about.

159
00:15:50.750 --> 00:15:52.750
And even though
she was no stranger to hardship,

160
00:15:54.458 --> 00:15:56.708
her humble eyes hardened.

161
00:15:58.417 --> 00:16:00.208
That's when she began to sigh.

162
00:16:01.083 --> 00:16:04.292
Finally, Pedro Páramo sent her away
to live with her sister.

163
00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:09.167
We lived with her in Colima.

164
00:16:09.667 --> 00:16:12.958
Some months later,
I asked Pedro Páramo about her.

165
00:16:14.833 --> 00:16:16.958
"How will they survive?" I would ask.

166
00:16:17.833 --> 00:16:20.500
And he would say,
"Let God take care of them."

167
00:16:23.583 --> 00:16:25.000
"Let God take care of them."

168
00:16:32.250 --> 00:16:33.917
When will you rest?

169
00:16:45.042 --> 00:16:46.125
Wake up!

170
00:17:06.125 --> 00:17:07.375
Why are you crying, Mama?

171
00:17:11.417 --> 00:17:12.667
Your father has died.

172
00:17:16.167 --> 00:17:17.667
They've killed your father.

173
00:17:27.125 --> 00:17:28.917
And you, Mother? Who killed you?

174
00:17:41.167 --> 00:17:43.000
<i>When will you rest?</i>

175
00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:46.208
Is something wrong, Doña Eduviges?

176
00:17:49.917 --> 00:17:51.875
It's Miguel Páramo's horse.

177
00:17:54.292 --> 00:17:56.958
Galloping along the road to Media Luna.

178
00:17:58.042 --> 00:17:59.792
So someone still lives at the Media Luna?

179
00:18:00.375 --> 00:18:03.375
No, no one lives there.

180
00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:06.583
I don't understand.

181
00:18:08.042 --> 00:18:10.375
- I don't hear a horse, either.
- No?

182
00:18:14.625 --> 00:18:17.250
Then it must be my sixth sense.

183
00:18:19.125 --> 00:18:20.667
A gift from God.

184
00:18:23.042 --> 00:18:24.917
Or perhaps a curse.

185
00:18:27.417 --> 00:18:28.750
Who was Miguel Páramo?

186
00:18:28.833 --> 00:18:30.292
Pedro Páramo's son.

187
00:18:31.625 --> 00:18:32.625
Another son?

188
00:18:33.792 --> 00:18:35.708
The only one he recognized as his own.

189
00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:41.625
He would spend some nights at my house.

190
00:18:42.125 --> 00:18:44.167
Until he met a girl from Contla.

191
00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:47.333
At night, he'd set off to visit her…

192
00:18:49.375 --> 00:18:51.667
and would return in the early dawn.

193
00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:54.833
But that night he didn't return.

194
00:18:57.667 --> 00:19:01.833
His horse was still passing by
when I felt someone knocking at my window.

195
00:19:03.750 --> 00:19:06.042
It might have just been my imagination.

196
00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:16.292
What happened?

197
00:19:17.083 --> 00:19:18.375
Did she break it off?

198
00:19:21.417 --> 00:19:22.417
That's not it.

199
00:19:23.458 --> 00:19:25.042
It's just that I lost the town.

200
00:19:28.042 --> 00:19:29.458
What are you saying, Miguel?

201
00:19:30.875 --> 00:19:32.250
There was a lot of fog.

202
00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:35.000
Or smoke.

203
00:19:35.833 --> 00:19:39.708
Or who knows what. What I do know,
is that Contla doesn't exist.

204
00:19:41.833 --> 00:19:45.417
I came to tell you
because I know you understand me.

205
00:19:46.792 --> 00:19:50.750
If I told anyone else in Comala,
they'd say I'm crazy.

206
00:19:53.208 --> 00:19:54.292
Like they always do.

207
00:19:59.750 --> 00:20:01.292
Not crazy, Miguel.

208
00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:06.000
You must be dead.

209
00:20:07.792 --> 00:20:11.167
Remember you were told
that horse was going to kill you one day.

210
00:20:11.958 --> 00:20:14.708
I only jumped over that stone fence
my father recently put up

211
00:20:14.792 --> 00:20:17.000
to avoid having to go
all the way around it.

212
00:20:19.083 --> 00:20:20.750
But there was nothing but smoke.

213
00:20:24.792 --> 00:20:25.792
Go.

214
00:20:32.125 --> 00:20:34.333
Go rest in peace, son.

215
00:20:38.833 --> 00:20:41.000
I'm grateful you came to say goodbye.

216
00:21:07.292 --> 00:21:09.000
Let us give thanks!

217
00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:14.167
Father, we want you to bless him!

218
00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:17.375
No. I won't do it.

219
00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:23.083
He was an evil man
and he won't enter the Kingdom of Heaven.

220
00:21:23.667 --> 00:21:26.333
God would be offended
if I intercede on his behalf.

221
00:22:15.125 --> 00:22:17.208
You know who they buried today?

222
00:22:21.042 --> 00:22:22.042
Yes, Uncle.

223
00:22:23.542 --> 00:22:25.833
You're sure it was him, right?

224
00:22:31.958 --> 00:22:33.125
Not completely sure, Uncle.

225
00:22:34.708 --> 00:22:35.833
I didn't see his face.

226
00:22:36.458 --> 00:22:38.375
He found me at night, and it was dark.

227
00:22:38.458 --> 00:22:42.333
So, how'd you know it was Miguel Páramo?

228
00:22:43.958 --> 00:22:45.000
Because he said so.

229
00:22:47.000 --> 00:22:49.792
He told me his name.
He said to not be afraid.

230
00:22:54.958 --> 00:22:59.625
But you knew he was responsible
for your father's death, didn't you?

231
00:23:01.125 --> 00:23:02.125
Yes, Uncle.

232
00:23:02.917 --> 00:23:06.083
So, what did you do to push him away?

233
00:23:09.792 --> 00:23:10.917
I didn't do anything.

234
00:23:15.458 --> 00:23:17.458
He said he had come to apologize…

235
00:23:18.458 --> 00:23:20.583
I thought about what you taught me.

236
00:23:23.250 --> 00:23:25.000
That we should never hate anyone.

237
00:23:28.292 --> 00:23:29.750
Then I felt him on top of me

238
00:23:33.042 --> 00:23:35.375
as he began doing bad things to me.

239
00:23:39.042 --> 00:23:40.625
I thought he was gonna kill me.

240
00:23:50.500 --> 00:23:54.042
Now he must be sinking
to the very depths of hell

241
00:23:56.083 --> 00:23:58.417
because that's
what I've asked all the saints for.

242
00:24:00.083 --> 00:24:02.458
You mustn't be too sure of that, child.

243
00:24:03.625 --> 00:24:06.500
Who knows how many are praying
for him right now.

244
00:24:11.667 --> 00:24:14.458
Besides, I've given him absolution.

245
00:24:16.833 --> 00:24:18.000
What are you saying, Uncle?

246
00:24:20.583 --> 00:24:24.250
Let's thank the Lord,
for He has taken him from this earth,

247
00:24:24.333 --> 00:24:26.250
where he has caused so much harm.

248
00:24:27.000 --> 00:24:29.458
Even if now
He has now received him in Heaven.

249
00:25:05.500 --> 00:25:07.375
Excuse me, Father Rentería.

250
00:25:08.333 --> 00:25:09.750
What do you need?

251
00:25:13.750 --> 00:25:15.292
My sister has died.

252
00:25:17.167 --> 00:25:18.458
How did it happen?

253
00:25:22.792 --> 00:25:24.833
She took her own life.

254
00:25:32.167 --> 00:25:34.208
What do you want me to do, María?

255
00:25:35.750 --> 00:25:38.542
I came to ask you to save her.

256
00:25:39.792 --> 00:25:41.667
But she killed herself.

257
00:25:43.667 --> 00:25:46.250
She acted in defiance of God.

258
00:25:47.750 --> 00:25:49.542
She failed at the last hour.

259
00:25:52.792 --> 00:25:56.833
So many good deeds
accumulated toward salvation,

260
00:25:57.833 --> 00:26:00.292
only to lose them in an instant.

261
00:26:00.375 --> 00:26:02.500
But she didn't lose them.

262
00:26:03.792 --> 00:26:06.833
She died choking on her own blood.

263
00:26:06.917 --> 00:26:08.542
Full of pain.

264
00:26:09.292 --> 00:26:10.417
And pain…

265
00:26:13.833 --> 00:26:17.250
You once told us something
about pain that I no longer remember.

266
00:26:18.458 --> 00:26:23.125
I mean, perhaps
by saying a few Gregorian Masses.

267
00:26:23.792 --> 00:26:26.792
But we'd need to ask for assistance,
send for priests.

268
00:26:28.500 --> 00:26:29.750
And that costs money.

269
00:26:30.917 --> 00:26:32.708
I don't have money.

270
00:26:34.167 --> 00:26:36.083
You know that, Father.

271
00:26:40.750 --> 00:26:42.542
Let's leave things as they are.

272
00:26:44.125 --> 00:26:45.625
Let's put our faith in God.

273
00:26:53.292 --> 00:26:54.292
Yes, Father.

274
00:27:39.167 --> 00:27:42.042
<i>…with your forgiveness</i>

275
00:27:43.458 --> 00:27:48.708
<i>Ave Maria</i>

276
00:27:49.917 --> 00:27:54.958
<i>Save her soul</i>

277
00:27:55.875 --> 00:28:00.708
<i>From purgatory</i>

278
00:28:01.458 --> 00:28:06.167
<i>With your forgiveness</i>

279
00:28:06.667 --> 00:28:11.625
<i>The light of the candle</i>

280
00:28:12.542 --> 00:28:16.875
<i>Grants eternal rest</i>

281
00:28:20.792 --> 00:28:23.083
Have you ever heard the moan of the dead?

282
00:28:34.500 --> 00:28:35.958
You'd better not, son.

283
00:28:53.333 --> 00:28:54.458
Doña Eduviges.

284
00:28:59.542 --> 00:29:00.583
Doña Eduviges?

285
00:29:05.208 --> 00:29:06.208
Doña Eduviges!

286
00:29:10.333 --> 00:29:11.583
Are you not coming back?

287
00:29:19.292 --> 00:29:20.625
<i>Let me go to my house!</i>

288
00:29:21.125 --> 00:29:24.292
<i>Let me go to say goodbye to my wife!
Let me go!</i>

289
00:29:25.167 --> 00:29:26.375
<i>Don Fulgor!</i>

290
00:29:29.042 --> 00:29:30.292
<i>No!</i>

291
00:30:00.333 --> 00:30:01.875
Doña Eduviges, is that you?

292
00:30:04.750 --> 00:30:06.083
I'm not Eduviges.

293
00:30:09.125 --> 00:30:10.583
My name is Damiana.

294
00:30:11.917 --> 00:30:13.333
I heard you were here,

295
00:30:14.417 --> 00:30:15.750
and I came to find you.

296
00:30:17.458 --> 00:30:18.792
Damiana Cisneros?

297
00:30:21.250 --> 00:30:23.042
Did you live in the Media Luna?

298
00:30:23.125 --> 00:30:26.375
That's where I live. That's why
it's taken me a while to get here.

299
00:30:27.708 --> 00:30:30.542
My mother told me about a Damiana
who cared for me when I was born.

300
00:30:31.875 --> 00:30:35.375
I've known you since you first
opened your eyes, Juan Preciado.

301
00:30:41.167 --> 00:30:44.083
I'll come with you.
I don't know what's happening here.

302
00:30:45.583 --> 00:30:47.417
Strange things are happening.

303
00:30:57.292 --> 00:30:58.875
I have to tell you…

304
00:31:00.375 --> 00:31:01.792
a few moments ago,

305
00:31:02.750 --> 00:31:03.875
from that very room…

306
00:31:05.333 --> 00:31:07.042
I heard someone wailing.

307
00:31:08.625 --> 00:31:10.333
As if in torment.

308
00:31:11.000 --> 00:31:13.833
Perhaps it's an echo trapped in there.

309
00:31:14.917 --> 00:31:19.625
In that room, they hanged Toribio Aldrete
a long time ago.

310
00:31:20.125 --> 00:31:23.083
Then they sealed the door
until his body dried out.

311
00:31:27.042 --> 00:31:28.708
I don't know how you got in.

312
00:31:30.042 --> 00:31:31.917
There's no key to open the door.

313
00:32:03.833 --> 00:32:07.083
No one's gonna say
you're not man enough, Don Fulgor.

314
00:32:07.875 --> 00:32:09.625
I know you are capable.

315
00:32:10.583 --> 00:32:14.208
And not on account of the authority
behind you, but on your own.

316
00:32:16.542 --> 00:32:20.583
But you and I are gonna use
this paper to wipe ourselves.

317
00:32:21.417 --> 00:32:23.500
Since that's all it's good for.

318
00:32:25.125 --> 00:32:29.500
And now that I know what this is about,
I can't help but laugh.

319
00:32:31.792 --> 00:32:34.625
Allegedly, "Toribio Aldrete"

320
00:32:34.708 --> 00:32:38.792
has not adjusted
to the limits of his property,

321
00:32:39.292 --> 00:32:43.333
and placed the dividing barriers

322
00:32:43.417 --> 00:32:45.917
on the land of the Media Luna,

323
00:32:46.500 --> 00:32:49.500
"property of Don Pedro Páramo."

324
00:32:55.417 --> 00:32:58.667
Doesn't it make you laugh too, Don Fulgor?

325
00:33:16.625 --> 00:33:18.458
Alleged "usufruct."

326
00:33:20.458 --> 00:33:23.375
"Usufruct," you say.

327
00:33:25.083 --> 00:33:29.083
Your <i>patrón </i>should be ashamed
for being so ignorant.

328
00:33:31.583 --> 00:33:32.625
Say, Viges…

329
00:33:34.500 --> 00:33:36.458
Can I use the room upstairs?

330
00:33:36.542 --> 00:33:38.083
Anything you need, Don Fulgor.

331
00:33:39.167 --> 00:33:40.917
Are your men going to stay the night?

332
00:33:43.583 --> 00:33:44.750
Just one of them.

333
00:33:47.875 --> 00:33:50.208
Don't worry about us and go to bed.

334
00:33:51.667 --> 00:33:53.125
Just leave us the key.

335
00:34:23.500 --> 00:34:24.625
Sit down, Fulgor.

336
00:34:24.708 --> 00:34:26.417
We can talk at ease.

337
00:34:28.500 --> 00:34:29.500
Why don't you sit?

338
00:34:30.167 --> 00:34:31.500
I'd prefer to stand, Pedro.

339
00:34:31.583 --> 00:34:34.708
Whatever you want.
But don't forget the "Don."

340
00:34:35.625 --> 00:34:37.458
- How's that going?
- What?

341
00:34:38.417 --> 00:34:39.917
You know what, the Media Luna.

342
00:34:40.625 --> 00:34:41.708
Not well.

343
00:34:42.500 --> 00:34:43.625
There is nothing left.

344
00:34:44.167 --> 00:34:45.958
We've sold the last of the livestock.

345
00:34:46.458 --> 00:34:50.625
Look. I won't get into details
because you don't even know the place.

346
00:34:50.708 --> 00:34:53.083
I mean, I've never seen you there.

347
00:34:53.167 --> 00:34:55.083
To date, we owe…

348
00:34:55.167 --> 00:34:56.250
Who do we owe?

349
00:34:56.875 --> 00:34:58.667
I don't care how much.
Just to whom we owe.

350
00:34:59.208 --> 00:35:02.667
Well, our greatest debt
is to the Preciado sisters.

351
00:35:03.542 --> 00:35:06.333
And then with the Fregoso,
and the Guzmán families.

352
00:35:07.417 --> 00:35:10.250
There's nothing left to pay them.
That's the issue.

353
00:35:10.333 --> 00:35:11.250
And why's that?

354
00:35:11.333 --> 00:35:14.417
Well, because your family used it all up.

355
00:35:15.708 --> 00:35:18.125
They took and took,
without giving anything back.

356
00:35:18.208 --> 00:35:21.125
I used to say to your late mother,
may God rest her soul,

357
00:35:22.083 --> 00:35:24.875
"You're gonna bleed this place dry."

358
00:35:24.958 --> 00:35:26.417
And that's what happened.

359
00:35:28.250 --> 00:35:32.000
Although someone may be interested
in buying the land, and they'd pay well.

360
00:35:34.333 --> 00:35:36.875
- Would that be you?
- How could you believe that?

361
00:35:36.958 --> 00:35:38.750
I'd believe anything, Fulgor.

362
00:35:42.792 --> 00:35:43.792
Okay.

363
00:35:44.208 --> 00:35:46.667
Tomorrow we'll start
putting our affairs in order.

364
00:35:47.333 --> 00:35:48.958
Beginning with the Preciado sisters.

365
00:35:49.458 --> 00:35:51.833
- You say that we owe them more?
- Yep.

366
00:35:52.458 --> 00:35:55.792
I understand one of them
went to live in the city. To Colima.

367
00:35:56.833 --> 00:36:02.333
And Lola, I mean, Doña Dolores, became
the sole owner of the Enmedio ranch.

368
00:36:02.417 --> 00:36:04.083
She's the one we'll have to pay.

369
00:36:08.583 --> 00:36:10.958
Tomorrow you'll ask Lola
for her hand in marriage.

370
00:36:11.042 --> 00:36:13.792
How do you think she'd want me?
I'm an old man.

371
00:36:13.875 --> 00:36:16.125
No, you'll ask her for me!

372
00:36:17.250 --> 00:36:19.083
After all, she has a certain charm.

373
00:36:20.583 --> 00:36:24.000
Tell her I'm very much in love with her.
Do that first thing tomorrow.

374
00:36:24.500 --> 00:36:25.500
Yep.

375
00:36:25.542 --> 00:36:27.750
Ask Father Rentería
to make the arrangements.

376
00:36:27.833 --> 00:36:29.208
How much money do you have?

377
00:36:29.292 --> 00:36:30.417
None, Don Pedro.

378
00:36:30.500 --> 00:36:33.167
Promise it to him.
Tell him we'll pay him when we can.

379
00:36:35.667 --> 00:36:36.917
Don't you want to sit down?

380
00:36:37.417 --> 00:36:38.875
I'll have a seat, Don Pedro.

381
00:36:38.958 --> 00:36:41.375
Truth is,
I'm beginning to like working with you.

382
00:36:42.708 --> 00:36:44.542
Tell Lola I love her.

383
00:36:44.625 --> 00:36:46.375
- That's important.
- Yeah.

384
00:36:46.458 --> 00:36:48.708
Truly, Sedano, I love her.

385
00:36:48.792 --> 00:36:50.750
For her eyes, you know?

386
00:36:51.875 --> 00:36:54.292
For her eyes, of course!

387
00:36:56.208 --> 00:36:58.542
Forgive me for blushing, Don Fulgor.

388
00:37:00.875 --> 00:37:05.417
But I never thought Don Pedro
would notice me.

389
00:37:06.292 --> 00:37:08.875
He can't sleep, thinking of you.

390
00:37:08.958 --> 00:37:10.833
But he could choose anyone.

391
00:37:11.750 --> 00:37:13.833
There are so many pretty girls in Comala.

392
00:37:15.792 --> 00:37:17.667
What will they say when they find out?

393
00:37:18.500 --> 00:37:20.375
He's a reserved man.

394
00:37:21.083 --> 00:37:26.250
Don Lucas Páramo, may he rest in peace,
told him you weren't worthy of him.

395
00:37:27.750 --> 00:37:30.167
And he kept quiet out of pure obedience.

396
00:37:31.417 --> 00:37:33.292
Now that his parents are gone,

397
00:37:34.167 --> 00:37:37.042
there's nothing to stand in the way.

398
00:37:37.667 --> 00:37:40.333
Let's set the wedding
for the day after tomorrow.

399
00:37:40.417 --> 00:37:41.500
What do you think?

400
00:37:42.583 --> 00:37:43.792
Isn't that rather soon?

401
00:37:50.917 --> 00:37:52.500
I don't have anything prepared.

402
00:37:53.167 --> 00:37:56.667
I'll need to arrange for the wedding
garments and write to my sister.

403
00:38:02.000 --> 00:38:05.375
No. I won't be ready before April 8th.

404
00:38:05.458 --> 00:38:07.083
Ask him to wait just a few days.

405
00:38:08.208 --> 00:38:10.542
He'd prefer to do it right now.

406
00:38:11.792 --> 00:38:15.375
Don't worry about the bridal goods,
we'll take care of it.

407
00:38:15.958 --> 00:38:20.292
Don Pedro's deceased mother
expects you to wear her dress.

408
00:38:21.167 --> 00:38:23.292
It's a family tradition.

409
00:38:25.292 --> 00:38:27.625
But there's something else
about that date.

410
00:38:28.375 --> 00:38:30.167
Women's issues, you know?

411
00:38:31.792 --> 00:38:34.167
I'm mortified
to say it out loud, Don Fulgor.

412
00:38:36.167 --> 00:38:37.167
It's my lunar cycle.

413
00:38:37.958 --> 00:38:39.083
I'm so embarrassed.

414
00:38:40.167 --> 00:38:41.458
And so what?

415
00:38:41.542 --> 00:38:45.208
Marriage isn't about whether
it's your time of the month or not.

416
00:38:46.042 --> 00:38:47.417
It's about loving each other.

417
00:38:47.917 --> 00:38:49.750
I don't think you're understanding me.

418
00:38:49.833 --> 00:38:53.458
I understand. The wedding
will be the day after tomorrow.

419
00:38:58.667 --> 00:39:02.375
Don't forget to tell the judge
that the property will be owned jointly.

420
00:39:04.125 --> 00:39:05.542
Jointly.

421
00:39:06.250 --> 00:39:07.250
Yes, Don Fulgor.

422
00:39:07.708 --> 00:39:08.750
Excuse me.

423
00:39:23.958 --> 00:39:25.542
Put water on to heat, Damiana.

424
00:39:26.042 --> 00:39:27.083
Yes, ma'am.

425
00:39:31.208 --> 00:39:34.792
I'll get this started as quickly
as possible. Maybe as early as tonight.

426
00:39:38.500 --> 00:39:41.125
Even so,
it's gonna last my usual three days.

427
00:39:43.625 --> 00:39:46.333
Thank you.
Thank you, God, for giving me Don Pedro.

428
00:39:49.542 --> 00:39:51.250
Even if later he despises me.

429
00:40:06.208 --> 00:40:09.167
So, Don Fulgor,
will the Media Luna be sold?

430
00:40:09.250 --> 00:40:10.958
Should we find another job?

431
00:40:12.042 --> 00:40:16.000
You don't know what work is.
But you'll learn. Don't worry.

432
00:40:17.417 --> 00:40:20.167
Don Fulgor, are you not leaving then?

433
00:40:21.250 --> 00:40:23.333
Didn't you say that Pedro was a lazy bum?

434
00:40:23.417 --> 00:40:26.167
That's what my <i>patrón,</i>
Don Lucas used to say.

435
00:40:26.250 --> 00:40:29.458
"That he would not take care of him
even in his old age," he said.

436
00:40:30.458 --> 00:40:32.542
My son turned out bad.

437
00:40:34.333 --> 00:40:36.458
From now on,
you will all call him "Don Pedro."

438
00:40:38.042 --> 00:40:40.708
She's been asked and more than willing.

439
00:40:41.833 --> 00:40:44.958
The priest wants 60 pesos
to overlook the marriage bans.

440
00:40:45.042 --> 00:40:47.250
I told him he'd be paid in due time.

441
00:40:47.875 --> 00:40:49.792
Didn't you ask Dolores for an advance?

442
00:40:50.292 --> 00:40:51.333
No, <i>patrón.</i>

443
00:40:51.958 --> 00:40:54.125
Truth is, I didn't dare.

444
00:40:54.625 --> 00:40:56.042
Fulgor, you're such a child.

445
00:40:57.083 --> 00:40:59.083
I didn't want to dampen her spirits.

446
00:41:00.958 --> 00:41:03.875
Next week, you'll go see Aldrete.

447
00:41:04.583 --> 00:41:07.958
Tell him to redo the fence.
He's on land that belongs to Media Luna.

448
00:41:08.542 --> 00:41:11.625
His measurements are accurate.
I'm sure of it.

449
00:41:11.708 --> 00:41:14.458
Well, tell him he made a mistake.
That he's figured wrong.

450
00:41:14.542 --> 00:41:16.375
Tear down the fencing if need be.

451
00:41:16.875 --> 00:41:17.958
And the laws?

452
00:41:18.458 --> 00:41:19.667
What laws, Fulgor?

453
00:41:20.167 --> 00:41:22.792
From now on,
we'll be the ones making the laws.

454
00:41:22.875 --> 00:41:27.500
File a complaint accusing him of usufruct.

455
00:41:28.500 --> 00:41:32.125
Remind him Lucas Páramo is dead.
He'll need to deal with me now.

456
00:41:32.208 --> 00:41:34.958
- Yes, <i>patrón. </i>Excuse me.
- Go ahead.

457
00:41:35.708 --> 00:41:37.417
"Usufruct"…

458
00:41:50.250 --> 00:41:53.958
No one can undermine
your manhood, Don Fulgor.

459
00:41:54.833 --> 00:41:59.542
But I'll be damned with that
son of a bitch of a <i>patrón </i>of yours!

460
00:42:04.000 --> 00:42:05.750
What are you going to do?

461
00:42:05.833 --> 00:42:07.375
Take you to rest, <i>patrón.</i>

462
00:42:07.458 --> 00:42:11.250
The day has not yet come
when tequila keeps me from walking.

463
00:42:16.083 --> 00:42:17.167
Go ahead, Toribio.

464
00:42:18.042 --> 00:42:19.208
"Usufruct."

465
00:42:27.708 --> 00:42:32.458
Don Fulgor, no offense,
but I prefer to sleep at home.

466
00:42:32.542 --> 00:42:34.542
For my wife's sake, so she won't worry.

467
00:42:35.083 --> 00:42:36.583
I don't want to trouble you.

468
00:42:36.667 --> 00:42:38.500
It's no trouble at all, Don Toribio.

469
00:42:39.917 --> 00:42:41.083
Let's go.

470
00:42:47.875 --> 00:42:49.625
What are you going to do?

471
00:42:51.208 --> 00:42:53.583
Let me go! Let me go home!

472
00:42:54.083 --> 00:42:56.500
Let me go to say goodbye to my wife!

473
00:42:56.583 --> 00:42:57.708
Let me go!

474
00:43:00.875 --> 00:43:02.250
Have mercy, Don Fulgor!

475
00:43:04.375 --> 00:43:05.417
Don Fulgor!

476
00:43:19.292 --> 00:43:22.208
Don Rubén, I'm glad you came.

477
00:43:22.292 --> 00:43:23.750
Cheers, Don Pedro.

478
00:43:23.833 --> 00:43:25.250
- Thank you.
- Excuse me.

479
00:43:31.292 --> 00:43:33.250
How are you guys doing?

480
00:43:33.917 --> 00:43:35.083
Excuse me.

481
00:43:37.250 --> 00:43:38.250
Gentlemen.

482
00:43:40.792 --> 00:43:41.958
Cheers, Don Pedro.

483
00:43:43.417 --> 00:43:46.500
The boys and I would like
to congratulate you.

484
00:43:46.583 --> 00:43:47.958
Thank you, Fulgor.

485
00:43:48.042 --> 00:43:49.042
Gentlemen.

486
00:43:52.583 --> 00:43:54.958
Is the thing with Toribio Aldrete
taken care of?

487
00:43:55.042 --> 00:43:56.792
That's settled, <i>patrón.</i>

488
00:43:57.792 --> 00:44:01.125
That leaves the Fregosos
and another issue we'll deal with later.

489
00:44:01.208 --> 00:44:02.458
What issue, Don Pedro?

490
00:44:02.542 --> 00:44:04.625
To find who killed my father.

491
00:44:06.375 --> 00:44:09.583
But save that for later.
Right now, I'm busy with my honeymoon.

492
00:44:11.417 --> 00:44:12.750
Let's go then, boys.

493
00:44:13.500 --> 00:44:15.208
- Excuse us, <i>patrón.</i>
- Sure, Fulgor.

494
00:44:19.083 --> 00:44:20.333
Run!

495
00:44:25.750 --> 00:44:27.292
Congratulations.

496
00:44:28.208 --> 00:44:29.417
- Counselor.
- Congratulations.

497
00:44:30.625 --> 00:44:32.208
Shall I take your dish, Father?

498
00:44:56.875 --> 00:44:57.958
Dorotea.

499
00:44:59.125 --> 00:45:00.125
Take this.

500
00:45:02.708 --> 00:45:05.208
God will repay you, Damiana.

501
00:45:05.708 --> 00:45:07.667
When you're done, go out the back.

502
00:45:10.625 --> 00:45:11.667
Excuse me.

503
00:45:16.917 --> 00:45:17.917
What?

504
00:45:18.917 --> 00:45:21.000
I'll be right back. What's going on?

505
00:45:21.542 --> 00:45:25.792
- What?
- He's drunk. He won't notice.

506
00:45:27.458 --> 00:45:29.458
What are you saying, Lola?

507
00:45:30.458 --> 00:45:32.375
How do you think it won't be noticed?

508
00:45:33.042 --> 00:45:35.167
I'm older than you and less dark-skinned.

509
00:45:35.250 --> 00:45:37.000
You can't see that in the dark.

510
00:45:38.583 --> 00:45:39.750
It can't be.

511
00:45:40.750 --> 00:45:42.458
Dolores, you must go.

512
00:45:42.542 --> 00:45:44.167
I didn't finish my menses.

513
00:45:45.792 --> 00:45:48.292
Do me that favor. I'll pay you back.

514
00:45:50.667 --> 00:45:51.875
Take my place.

515
00:45:53.042 --> 00:45:55.167
- That's what we're friends for, right?
- No!

516
00:46:11.667 --> 00:46:13.625
This town is full of echoes.

517
00:46:17.375 --> 00:46:22.750
There was a time when I could hear
the commotion of a party.

518
00:46:24.000 --> 00:46:26.167
The noise made it all the way out
to the Media Luna.

519
00:46:27.875 --> 00:46:30.125
I came down to see
what the fuss was about,

520
00:46:31.333 --> 00:46:34.000
and I saw this,
what we're seeing right now.

521
00:46:34.542 --> 00:46:36.792
The streets as empty as they are now.

522
00:46:37.875 --> 00:46:39.417
But I don't get scared anymore.

523
00:46:39.500 --> 00:46:43.208
I think the day will come
when these echoes will die out.

524
00:46:45.875 --> 00:46:49.417
If they are echoes,
they must come from a voice.

525
00:46:50.958 --> 00:46:52.000
You will hear them.

526
00:46:52.500 --> 00:46:55.792
As if they were coming out
of some crack or under the stones.

527
00:47:01.208 --> 00:47:03.458
This was the Páramos' house.

528
00:47:04.042 --> 00:47:07.125
Since his grandparents came to Comala.

529
00:47:13.000 --> 00:47:17.542
Although, Don Pedro lived
most of his life in the Media Luna,

530
00:47:18.750 --> 00:47:19.917
and I with him.

531
00:47:22.917 --> 00:47:25.875
I became the boss of all his maids.

532
00:47:25.958 --> 00:47:28.083
Just because I knew how to be respected.

533
00:47:28.917 --> 00:47:31.875
I was the only one
who didn't allow him into my bed.

534
00:47:37.375 --> 00:47:38.833
Are you going to the Media Luna?

535
00:47:40.375 --> 00:47:42.208
You'll have somewhere to rest there.

536
00:47:46.875 --> 00:47:51.208
You can't imagine the crowd of souls
that roam these streets.

537
00:47:52.250 --> 00:47:54.833
They are the souls
of those who died unforgiven

538
00:47:54.917 --> 00:47:56.375
and still suffer.

539
00:47:57.167 --> 00:47:59.375
Especially the ones
Pedro Páramo had killed

540
00:47:59.458 --> 00:48:01.208
after his father's murder.

541
00:48:02.875 --> 00:48:03.917
Were there that many?

542
00:48:04.000 --> 00:48:05.000
Yes.

543
00:48:11.292 --> 00:48:13.208
Did my mother also tell you I was coming?

544
00:48:16.750 --> 00:48:19.500
By the way, how is your mother?

545
00:48:20.167 --> 00:48:21.167
She died.

546
00:48:22.625 --> 00:48:24.083
I thought you would've known.

547
00:48:26.792 --> 00:48:28.292
How would I have known?

548
00:48:30.958 --> 00:48:33.083
It's been years since I've known anything.

549
00:48:34.083 --> 00:48:35.792
Then how did you find me?

550
00:48:39.958 --> 00:48:41.250
Are you alive, Damiana?

551
00:48:48.458 --> 00:48:49.458
Damiana?

552
00:48:51.542 --> 00:48:52.792
Damiana Cisneros!

553
00:48:54.833 --> 00:48:56.042
Damiana!

554
00:49:18.208 --> 00:49:19.500
Here, Damiana.

555
00:49:32.000 --> 00:49:33.708
Why are you sighing, Doloritas?

556
00:49:34.375 --> 00:49:38.000
I wish I were a vulture
so I could fly to where my sister lives.

557
00:49:38.917 --> 00:49:41.250
Of course, Doña Doloritas.

558
00:49:41.750 --> 00:49:43.667
You'll leave immediately
to go see your sister.

559
00:49:44.542 --> 00:49:45.542
Let's head back.

560
00:49:46.333 --> 00:49:47.667
Get her bags packed.

561
00:49:48.458 --> 00:49:49.792
It's the least I could do.

562
00:49:57.792 --> 00:50:00.292
<i>My mother lived longing for Comala.</i>

563
00:50:01.708 --> 00:50:02.917
<i>For the return</i>

564
00:50:04.167 --> 00:50:06.667
<i>to the place
where you'd want to live for eternity.</i>

565
00:50:08.625 --> 00:50:10.375
Isn't that Filoteo Aréchiga?

566
00:50:11.583 --> 00:50:13.500
That's him. Pretend not to notice.

567
00:50:15.042 --> 00:50:16.500
Do you think he's following us?

568
00:50:17.000 --> 00:50:18.375
He better not be.

569
00:50:18.458 --> 00:50:21.292
Rumor has it he's the one
who finds girls for Don Pedro.

570
00:50:21.875 --> 00:50:22.958
- Is that so?
- Go in there.

571
00:50:23.042 --> 00:50:24.042
Excuse me.

572
00:50:28.250 --> 00:50:29.250
Excuse me!

573
00:50:41.375 --> 00:50:43.500
I was just passing by.

574
00:50:48.083 --> 00:50:50.333
Don Pedro had no intention of killing me.

575
00:50:51.167 --> 00:50:54.708
He just wanted to know if I was at
the wedding where his father was killed.

576
00:50:56.458 --> 00:50:58.833
He's been getting rid of
all the guests to the party.

577
00:51:01.917 --> 00:51:03.667
But he just wanted to scare me!

578
00:51:14.042 --> 00:51:15.542
Heaven is vast.

579
00:51:44.250 --> 00:51:45.333
What're you doing here?

580
00:51:46.167 --> 00:51:47.375
Are you not dead?

581
00:51:50.208 --> 00:51:51.375
He's drunk.

582
00:51:53.458 --> 00:51:54.958
He's just scared.

583
00:51:55.667 --> 00:51:56.833
Come in.

584
00:52:23.000 --> 00:52:24.083
Are you sick?

585
00:52:25.167 --> 00:52:27.292
I just want to go back
to where I came from.

586
00:52:27.792 --> 00:52:29.458
You'd better wait until tomorrow.

587
00:52:31.667 --> 00:52:33.708
All roads are tangled with brush.

588
00:52:35.000 --> 00:52:36.000
You could get lost.

589
00:52:37.667 --> 00:52:39.292
Tomorrow, I'll get you on track.

590
00:53:07.917 --> 00:53:08.958
Who could he be?

591
00:53:11.958 --> 00:53:13.375
How did he get here?

592
00:53:16.208 --> 00:53:17.542
He must be lost.

593
00:53:20.417 --> 00:53:22.125
Why don't you go to sleep…

594
00:53:24.125 --> 00:53:25.667
and let me rest?

595
00:53:33.667 --> 00:53:34.667
Look at him.

596
00:53:39.583 --> 00:53:41.333
Look how he squirms…

597
00:53:44.042 --> 00:53:45.667
as if he were cursed.

598
00:53:56.542 --> 00:53:59.458
He must be someone who owes many deaths.

599
00:54:14.042 --> 00:54:15.417
It's orange blossom water.

600
00:54:16.875 --> 00:54:17.917
It will calm your fears.

601
00:54:23.583 --> 00:54:24.917
No need to worry about me.

602
00:54:31.125 --> 00:54:32.500
How can I get out of here?

603
00:54:32.583 --> 00:54:33.583
To go where?

604
00:54:34.625 --> 00:54:35.833
Anywhere.

605
00:54:38.083 --> 00:54:39.792
There's a multitude of roads.

606
00:54:45.208 --> 00:54:46.625
Where did your husband go?

607
00:54:49.542 --> 00:54:50.625
He's not my husband.

608
00:54:52.250 --> 00:54:53.250
He's my brother.

609
00:55:00.250 --> 00:55:01.750
He doesn't want to believe it.

610
00:55:06.375 --> 00:55:08.583
But don't you think I'm scary?

611
00:55:11.208 --> 00:55:12.292
Come closer.

612
00:55:15.125 --> 00:55:16.292
Look at my face.

613
00:55:22.000 --> 00:55:23.500
What is it you want me to see?

614
00:55:27.792 --> 00:55:29.208
Don't you see the sin on me?

615
00:55:34.958 --> 00:55:37.042
Don't you see the rash?

616
00:55:41.375 --> 00:55:42.958
And that's just on the outside.

617
00:55:47.958 --> 00:55:50.000
Inside, I'm an ocean of mud.

618
00:55:53.792 --> 00:55:54.833
If you don't mind…

619
00:55:57.750 --> 00:55:59.292
I'd like to get some sleep.

620
00:56:47.292 --> 00:56:48.375
He's not coming back.

621
00:56:50.750 --> 00:56:51.792
I beg your pardon?

622
00:56:51.875 --> 00:56:53.542
I could see it in his eyes.

623
00:56:56.500 --> 00:56:59.250
He was just waiting for someone
to show up so he could leave.

624
00:57:02.333 --> 00:57:04.333
Now you'll have to look after me.

625
00:57:06.083 --> 00:57:07.083
Or what?

626
00:57:09.250 --> 00:57:10.667
Don't you want to take care of me?

627
00:57:26.708 --> 00:57:28.250
Come sleep next to me.

628
00:57:29.500 --> 00:57:30.542
I'm fine where I am.

629
00:57:32.125 --> 00:57:34.000
You'd be better here on the bed.

630
00:57:34.833 --> 00:57:36.833
The ticks will eat you alive down there.

631
00:59:50.667 --> 00:59:52.917
<i>Pedro Páramo laid waste to everything.</i>

632
00:59:53.667 --> 00:59:56.750
<i>That's unforgivable.
And what about the rapes?</i>

633
00:59:57.417 --> 00:59:59.417
<i>We were also afraid of him.</i>

634
01:00:00.750 --> 01:00:04.417
<i>We have to wait until he dies.
You won't get anything from here.</i>

635
01:00:18.167 --> 01:00:21.042
<i>Pray for us, Juan Preciado.</i>

636
01:00:21.708 --> 01:00:24.167
<i>Pray for me, Juan Preciado.</i>

637
01:00:55.500 --> 01:00:59.167
<i>You expect me to believe you died
of suffocation, Juan Preciado?</i>

638
01:01:00.417 --> 01:01:02.875
<i>I found you twisted up.</i>

639
01:01:03.375 --> 01:01:06.125
<i>Like someone who's died of fright.</i>

640
01:01:09.083 --> 01:01:10.375
<i>It's true, Dorotea.</i>

641
01:01:11.375 --> 01:01:13.083
<i>It was the murmurs that killed me.</i>

642
01:01:14.083 --> 01:01:15.625
<i>The fear came late,</i>

643
01:01:16.458 --> 01:01:18.375
<i>and that's when my soul froze.</i>

644
01:01:21.333 --> 01:01:22.417
<i>You hear?</i>

645
01:01:23.375 --> 01:01:25.583
<i>It's raining up there.</i>

646
01:01:26.542 --> 01:01:29.167
<i>Don't you feel the rain beating down?</i>

647
01:01:31.042 --> 01:01:33.583
<i>It feels as if someone's walking
on top of us.</i>

648
01:01:34.708 --> 01:01:37.167
<i>Try to think pleasant thoughts</i>

649
01:01:37.250 --> 01:01:40.583
<i>because we're going to be buried here
for a long time.</i>

650
01:01:49.125 --> 01:01:50.750
Fall, sweet rain, fall.

651
01:01:51.375 --> 01:01:53.583
Keep coming till you're exhausted.

652
01:02:23.000 --> 01:02:25.458
Where are you coming from
this time of day, boy?

653
01:02:26.208 --> 01:02:27.333
I was out milking.

654
01:02:28.167 --> 01:02:29.167
Milking who?

655
01:02:29.625 --> 01:02:30.917
Can't you guess?

656
01:02:31.000 --> 01:02:34.750
It must be Dorotea, La Cuarraca.

657
01:02:34.833 --> 01:02:38.917
- She's the only one who likes babies.
- You're an idiot, Fulgor.

658
01:02:41.667 --> 01:02:42.750
Margarita.

659
01:02:44.042 --> 01:02:45.833
Where have you been, Miguel?

660
01:02:46.708 --> 01:02:49.875
Out and about, visiting mothers.

661
01:02:50.875 --> 01:02:51.875
Listen.

662
01:02:52.875 --> 01:02:55.375
Do you know someone named Dorotea?
One they call "La Cuarraca?"

663
01:02:56.542 --> 01:02:58.708
If you want to see her,
she's right outside.

664
01:03:00.500 --> 01:03:03.250
She rises early to come here
for some breakfast.

665
01:03:03.333 --> 01:03:05.958
She's a poor woman who lives on handouts.

666
01:03:06.458 --> 01:03:08.292
Damned old man.

667
01:03:09.083 --> 01:03:10.167
Dorotea!

668
01:03:11.625 --> 01:03:13.625
Come here. I've got a deal for you.

669
01:03:20.083 --> 01:03:22.000
Bring on those eggs.

670
01:03:24.083 --> 01:03:27.000
From now on, you'll feed
that woman the same thing as me.

671
01:03:27.833 --> 01:03:29.875
Don't be stingy.

672
01:03:40.292 --> 01:03:41.542
Fulgor!

673
01:03:46.042 --> 01:03:48.167
- Excuse me, <i>patrón.</i>
- How are we doing?

674
01:03:49.125 --> 01:03:52.417
We drove the cattle from Enmedio Ranch
past what used to be the Fregosos'.

675
01:03:52.917 --> 01:03:55.708
And the Fregosos',
we ran them to the hills of Vilmayo.

676
01:03:55.792 --> 01:03:56.792
Okay.

677
01:03:58.583 --> 01:04:00.000
What's wrong with you?

678
01:04:01.667 --> 01:04:05.250
Someone came by this morning,
accusing your son Miguel of killing a man.

679
01:04:08.125 --> 01:04:09.667
Pretend it was me.

680
01:04:09.750 --> 01:04:12.250
Anything he does, put the blame on me.

681
01:04:13.750 --> 01:04:16.375
Miguel's gonna cause you
a lot of headaches, <i>patrón.</i>

682
01:04:16.458 --> 01:04:17.792
He likes trouble.

683
01:04:17.875 --> 01:04:20.958
Give him space. He's just a child.

684
01:04:21.625 --> 01:04:22.667
How old is he now?

685
01:04:23.167 --> 01:04:25.583
He must be 17. Right, Fulgor?

686
01:04:25.667 --> 01:04:26.667
Could be.

687
01:04:27.583 --> 01:04:29.958
But he's so violent and always in a hurry.

688
01:04:30.458 --> 01:04:33.833
Sometimes it feels like
he's racing against time.

689
01:04:35.125 --> 01:04:37.375
He'll end up losing. You'll see.

690
01:04:38.583 --> 01:04:40.000
He's still a baby, Fulgor.

691
01:04:40.583 --> 01:04:42.208
Whatever you say, <i>patrón.</i>

692
01:04:43.125 --> 01:04:46.750
But the woman who came claiming
that your son killed her husband

693
01:04:46.833 --> 01:04:48.625
was beyond hysterical.

694
01:04:49.792 --> 01:04:50.833
Who was it?

695
01:04:52.083 --> 01:04:53.375
People I don't know.

696
01:04:53.958 --> 01:04:57.375
Don't worry about it, Fulgor.
Those people don't exist.

697
01:04:58.917 --> 01:05:01.167
Keep calm. Let's do nothing.

698
01:05:02.250 --> 01:05:03.583
All right.

699
01:05:03.667 --> 01:05:04.708
Excuse me, <i>patrón.</i>

700
01:05:09.417 --> 01:05:12.792
<i>My mother used to tell me
about the green plains and the clouds.</i>

701
01:05:14.625 --> 01:05:16.875
<i>And yet, she was unable
to return to die here.</i>

702
01:05:19.000 --> 01:05:21.500
<i>Even for that, she sent me in her stead.</i>

703
01:05:23.583 --> 01:05:24.958
<i>It's strange, Dorotea.</i>

704
01:05:26.958 --> 01:05:28.958
<i>How I never even got to see the sky.</i>

705
01:05:30.750 --> 01:05:33.042
<i>I lost all interest in Heaven</i>

706
01:05:33.125 --> 01:05:37.375
<i>when Father Rentería assured me
I'd never know God's glory</i>

707
01:05:39.125 --> 01:05:41.083
<i>on account of my sins.</i>

708
01:05:41.875 --> 01:05:44.458
<i>But he shouldn't have told me that.</i>

709
01:05:45.958 --> 01:05:48.667
<i>When they slam a door in your face,</i>

710
01:05:49.375 --> 01:05:52.292
<i>and the only one left open
takes you to hell…</i>

711
01:05:53.250 --> 01:05:55.167
<i>it would be better to not have been born.</i>

712
01:06:22.875 --> 01:06:26.000
I'm told Doña Susana
and her father left Mascota.

713
01:06:26.083 --> 01:06:27.208
Where did they go?

714
01:06:27.292 --> 01:06:31.833
I've gone all over the range asking.
Some say this way, others say that way.

715
01:06:32.333 --> 01:06:33.875
I can't find them, Don Pedro.

716
01:06:33.958 --> 01:06:36.167
Spare no expense. Keep looking!

717
01:06:36.250 --> 01:06:39.090
- The earth couldn't have swallowed them!
- Whatever you say, Don Pedro.

718
01:07:58.500 --> 01:08:01.792
Not like that!
Turn him, and take him in headfirst.

719
01:08:23.042 --> 01:08:24.042
What did they do to him?

720
01:08:26.083 --> 01:08:27.375
No one did anything to him.

721
01:08:28.958 --> 01:08:30.333
He found death all by himself.

722
01:08:30.833 --> 01:08:32.458
His horse killed him, Don Pedro.

723
01:08:35.000 --> 01:08:36.542
I'm beginning to pay.

724
01:08:39.792 --> 01:08:42.292
Better start early, to finish sooner.

725
01:08:46.750 --> 01:08:50.000
When you can,
put that animal out of its misery.

726
01:08:50.083 --> 01:08:51.333
Indeed, Don Pedro.

727
01:09:09.500 --> 01:09:12.917
Don Pedro,
Father Rentería would like to see you.

728
01:09:13.417 --> 01:09:14.542
Now?

729
01:09:17.000 --> 01:09:18.208
Tell him to come in.

730
01:09:20.333 --> 01:09:21.917
Father, come in.

731
01:09:25.542 --> 01:09:27.000
Sorry to interrupt.

732
01:09:30.167 --> 01:09:34.667
Don Pedro, I was told that his mother
died giving birth and that he's yours.

733
01:09:35.167 --> 01:09:36.292
Here he is.

734
01:09:40.375 --> 01:09:41.833
Why don't you keep him, Father?

735
01:09:42.833 --> 01:09:43.833
Make him a priest.

736
01:09:45.083 --> 01:09:48.792
Not with the blood inside him.
I don't want that responsibility.

737
01:09:52.083 --> 01:09:53.792
You think I have bad blood?

738
01:09:56.458 --> 01:09:58.500
I really do, Don Pedro.

739
01:10:00.208 --> 01:10:01.875
I'll prove you wrong.

740
01:10:02.542 --> 01:10:05.417
Leave him here. There are plenty
of people who'll take care of him.

741
01:10:05.500 --> 01:10:06.583
That's what I figured.

742
01:10:06.667 --> 01:10:09.417
At least with you,
he won't lack sustenance.

743
01:10:10.667 --> 01:10:11.792
Damiana!

744
01:10:19.292 --> 01:10:20.708
Come take care of this thing.

745
01:10:21.208 --> 01:10:22.208
It's my son.

746
01:10:29.625 --> 01:10:33.000
Here's to the late mother and to you.

747
01:10:33.500 --> 01:10:34.542
And to the infant?

748
01:10:35.500 --> 01:10:37.375
To him as well. Why not?

749
01:10:39.458 --> 01:10:40.458
Here.

750
01:11:15.250 --> 01:11:17.375
Eternal rest grant unto him, O Lord,

751
01:11:17.458 --> 01:11:19.750
and let perpetual light shine upon him.

752
01:11:26.875 --> 01:11:28.958
Have mercy on Thy servant, O Lord.

753
01:11:29.042 --> 01:11:31.875
May he rest in peace. Amen.

754
01:11:45.500 --> 01:11:47.417
I know you hated him, Father.

755
01:11:48.750 --> 01:11:50.458
And rightly so.

756
01:11:50.958 --> 01:11:52.708
Your brother's murder.

757
01:11:54.042 --> 01:11:55.792
The case of your niece, Ana.

758
01:11:56.333 --> 01:11:57.792
But forget all that now.

759
01:11:58.750 --> 01:12:02.250
Think it over and forgive him,
as perhaps God has forgiven him.

760
01:12:07.458 --> 01:12:09.792
Accept this as a donation to your church.

761
01:12:29.250 --> 01:12:31.417
Thou wilt know if this is the price.

762
01:12:33.750 --> 01:12:35.875
For my part, Lord, condemn him.

763
01:12:42.250 --> 01:12:43.375
O Mary.

764
01:12:43.458 --> 01:12:44.875
Conceived without sin.

765
01:12:45.750 --> 01:12:47.208
Tell me your sins, my child.

766
01:12:47.292 --> 01:12:50.542
I confess, Father, that last night
I slept with Pedro Páramo.

767
01:12:50.625 --> 01:12:51.708
What else?

768
01:12:51.792 --> 01:12:53.750
I'm going to have Pedro Páramo's child.

769
01:12:54.375 --> 01:12:56.667
I gave my daughter to Pedro Páramo.

770
01:12:56.750 --> 01:12:59.458
May the evil you have done serve for…

771
01:12:59.542 --> 01:13:00.750
Serve to elevate…

772
01:13:00.833 --> 01:13:02.625
Merciful Father.

773
01:13:09.458 --> 01:13:11.125
Hail purest Mary.

774
01:13:12.542 --> 01:13:14.958
Conceived without sin.

775
01:13:15.667 --> 01:13:17.833
So now you're getting drunk?

776
01:13:20.250 --> 01:13:25.542
Now that I can't cause him any harm…

777
01:13:27.500 --> 01:13:28.667
I can say

778
01:13:29.500 --> 01:13:33.792
I was the one who got all those girls

779
01:13:34.292 --> 01:13:37.458
for the late Miguelito Páramo.

780
01:13:39.125 --> 01:13:40.542
You took them to him?

781
01:13:41.833 --> 01:13:43.167
Sometimes I did.

782
01:13:44.333 --> 01:13:46.792
Other times, I'd just set it up.

783
01:13:47.333 --> 01:13:52.958
Or I told him when they'd be all alone
so he could take them by surprise.

784
01:14:02.000 --> 01:14:03.000
Father…

785
01:14:08.833 --> 01:14:12.208
Father, aren't you going to give me
any penance?

786
01:14:16.125 --> 01:14:18.625
What would you have me do
with you, Dorotea?

787
01:14:21.458 --> 01:14:25.083
Be your own judge.
See if you can forgive yourself.

788
01:14:27.375 --> 01:14:29.417
I can't, Father.

789
01:14:30.583 --> 01:14:32.000
But you can.

790
01:14:32.500 --> 01:14:34.333
How many times have you come here

791
01:14:34.417 --> 01:14:37.500
asking me to send you
to Heaven when you die?

792
01:14:38.750 --> 01:14:42.500
You were hoping
to find your son there, right, Dorotea?

793
01:14:44.333 --> 01:14:45.333
Well,

794
01:14:46.708 --> 01:14:49.250
you won't be going to Heaven anymore.

795
01:14:51.042 --> 01:14:53.000
But may God forgive you.

796
01:14:58.083 --> 01:15:00.125
<i>Her eyelashes were already still.</i>

797
01:15:00.625 --> 01:15:02.208
<i>And her heart was still as well.</i>

798
01:15:02.292 --> 01:15:04.583
<i>Was that you saying all that, Dorotea?</i>

799
01:15:05.208 --> 01:15:06.792
<i>Are they still frightening you?</i>

800
01:15:06.875 --> 01:15:09.417
<i>There is nothing but a dead thing here.</i>

801
01:15:09.917 --> 01:15:11.500
<i>I heard someone speaking.</i>

802
01:15:12.083 --> 01:15:13.417
<i>A woman's voice.</i>

803
01:15:13.500 --> 01:15:14.958
<i>I thought it was you.</i>

804
01:15:15.458 --> 01:15:17.542
<i>It must be the woman who talks to herself.</i>

805
01:15:18.042 --> 01:15:19.917
<i>The one in the large grave.</i>

806
01:15:20.000 --> 01:15:21.500
<i>Doña Susanita.</i>

807
01:15:22.583 --> 01:15:24.750
<i>She's buried here beside us.</i>

808
01:15:25.417 --> 01:15:27.625
<i>What happens with old corpses</i>

809
01:15:27.708 --> 01:15:32.292
<i>is that when moisture reaches them,
they begin to stir.</i>

810
01:15:32.375 --> 01:15:33.542
<i>And they wake up.</i>

811
01:15:34.292 --> 01:15:35.375
<i>And who is she?</i>

812
01:15:36.958 --> 01:15:39.875
<i>Pedro Páramo's last wife.</i>

813
01:15:40.792 --> 01:15:42.833
<i>They say she was insane.</i>

814
01:15:44.750 --> 01:15:46.000
<i>What is she saying?</i>

815
01:15:47.583 --> 01:15:48.583
<i>She just complains.</i>

816
01:15:50.917 --> 01:15:52.250
<i>Maybe he made her suffer.</i>

817
01:15:54.958 --> 01:15:56.250
<i>Don't believe that.</i>

818
01:15:56.917 --> 01:15:58.000
<i>He loved her.</i>

819
01:15:59.208 --> 01:16:03.375
<i>I'm about to say that he loved her
more than any other woman.</i>

820
01:16:22.250 --> 01:16:23.500
No. You lost.

821
01:17:06.833 --> 01:17:09.708
<i>Now I remember
her mother died of consumption.</i>

822
01:17:12.042 --> 01:17:15.250
<i>It was then that she
and her father disappeared.</i>

823
01:17:19.750 --> 01:17:23.792
<i>When they brought her
to Pedro Páramo, many years later,</i>

824
01:17:23.875 --> 01:17:26.000
<i>she was suffering.</i>

825
01:17:28.750 --> 01:17:30.042
<i>His love was such</i>

826
01:17:30.125 --> 01:17:33.875
<i>that he spent his remaining years
slumped over in an old chair,</i>

827
01:17:34.958 --> 01:17:38.708
<i>gazing down the road
where she was taken to the cemetery.</i>

828
01:17:42.917 --> 01:17:44.083
It won't take long.

829
01:17:47.292 --> 01:17:48.292
It won't take long.

830
01:17:54.583 --> 01:17:55.583
Excuse me.

831
01:18:00.792 --> 01:18:03.000
Here are the figures
you asked for, Don Pedro.

832
01:18:04.250 --> 01:18:05.333
Oh goodness.

833
01:18:09.667 --> 01:18:10.875
Do you know who's back?

834
01:18:11.500 --> 01:18:12.958
Bartolomé San Juan.

835
01:18:15.583 --> 01:18:16.500
How come?

836
01:18:16.583 --> 01:18:18.458
That's what I want to know.

837
01:18:19.625 --> 01:18:21.833
He went straight
to that old house of yours,

838
01:18:21.917 --> 01:18:24.083
as if you'd already rented
the place to him.

839
01:18:25.083 --> 01:18:26.792
At least, that's how he acted.

840
01:18:27.792 --> 01:18:29.875
I'll clear things up tomorrow, Don Pedro.

841
01:18:31.250 --> 01:18:32.417
Did they both come?

842
01:18:32.500 --> 01:18:33.500
Yep.

843
01:18:33.833 --> 01:18:34.917
He and his wife.

844
01:18:35.417 --> 01:18:36.667
How did you know?

845
01:18:36.750 --> 01:18:38.000
Wouldn't it be his daughter?

846
01:18:40.500 --> 01:18:44.833
Well… considering the way he treats her,
she seems like she's his wife.

847
01:18:52.833 --> 01:18:53.875
It's Susana.

848
01:18:55.000 --> 01:18:56.167
For sure, Fulgor.

849
01:18:58.708 --> 01:19:02.167
We found them
near the abandoned La Andrómeda mines.

850
01:19:08.042 --> 01:19:11.500
What must have brought them here
are the rumors of people up in arms.

851
01:19:12.000 --> 01:19:13.125
Oh, maybe.

852
01:19:13.792 --> 01:19:16.000
They say it's getting quite serious.

853
01:19:16.917 --> 01:19:19.667
He must've wanted to bring her
to a place that's alive.

854
01:19:21.583 --> 01:19:22.625
Go to bed, Fulgor.

855
01:19:23.917 --> 01:19:25.667
With your permission, <i>patrón.</i>

856
01:19:33.708 --> 01:19:36.042
This town tastes of misfortune.

857
01:19:37.792 --> 01:19:40.292
We'll find no salvation here.

858
01:19:41.583 --> 01:19:42.708
I can feel it.

859
01:19:46.542 --> 01:19:50.042
I had imagined that all
he was giving us would not be free.

860
01:19:52.458 --> 01:19:54.583
You know what Pedro Páramo asked me?

861
01:19:58.542 --> 01:20:00.500
He said that all he wants from me

862
01:20:01.250 --> 01:20:02.500
is you.

863
01:20:03.708 --> 01:20:05.708
That you've been my best work.

864
01:20:07.167 --> 01:20:10.000
He says you played together as kids.

865
01:20:10.833 --> 01:20:13.167
That you even swam together in the river.

866
01:20:14.792 --> 01:20:17.833
Had I known,
I would've whipped you to death.

867
01:20:20.167 --> 01:20:21.208
I don't doubt it.

868
01:20:24.958 --> 01:20:27.792
So, you are willing to sleep with him?

869
01:20:28.625 --> 01:20:30.708
- Yes, Bartolomé.
- Don't call me Bartolomé.

870
01:20:32.583 --> 01:20:33.750
I'm your father!

871
01:20:37.542 --> 01:20:39.000
I've told him you're a widow.

872
01:20:40.208 --> 01:20:42.375
And you still live with your husband.

873
01:20:44.417 --> 01:20:47.417
Or at least that's how you act.

874
01:20:51.750 --> 01:20:53.542
I've tried to dissuade him.

875
01:20:54.417 --> 01:20:57.167
But he scowls when I talk to him.

876
01:20:59.417 --> 01:21:00.792
He's pure evil.

877
01:21:01.750 --> 01:21:03.167
That's what Pedro Páramo is.

878
01:21:07.833 --> 01:21:09.125
And who am I?

879
01:21:10.333 --> 01:21:11.417
You're my daughter.

880
01:21:12.375 --> 01:21:13.375
Mine.

881
01:21:14.542 --> 01:21:16.500
The daughter of Bartolomé San Juan.

882
01:21:23.917 --> 01:21:25.250
What have we done?

883
01:21:27.292 --> 01:21:29.375
Why has our soul rotted away?

884
01:21:32.417 --> 01:21:33.542
It is not true.

885
01:21:35.542 --> 01:21:37.833
- It is not true.
- What is not true?

886
01:21:39.375 --> 01:21:40.625
Have you gone mad?

887
01:21:43.458 --> 01:21:44.542
Of course, Bartolomé.

888
01:21:46.208 --> 01:21:47.458
Didn't you know?

889
01:22:10.458 --> 01:22:14.458
<i>Did you know, Fulgor, that she's the most
beautiful woman ever born to this earth?</i>

890
01:22:16.667 --> 01:22:18.792
<i>I began to believe I'd lost her forever.</i>

891
01:22:20.333 --> 01:22:22.500
<i>But I have no intention
of losing her again.</i>

892
01:22:25.292 --> 01:22:27.458
- You understand me, Fulgor?
- I do.

893
01:22:29.542 --> 01:22:31.583
Tell her father
we'll provide what he needs

894
01:22:31.667 --> 01:22:33.208
to keep working in the mines.

895
01:22:34.542 --> 01:22:37.862
I imagine it'll be easier to make the old
man disappear over there, don't you think?

896
01:22:38.333 --> 01:22:39.458
Could be.

897
01:22:40.292 --> 01:22:41.500
We need it to be.

898
01:22:43.083 --> 01:22:44.708
She has to be orphaned.

899
01:22:46.083 --> 01:22:48.083
It's our duty to support those in need.

900
01:22:50.875 --> 01:22:54.083
And what if she finds out?

901
01:22:55.125 --> 01:22:56.333
Who's going to tell her?

902
01:22:57.208 --> 01:22:59.208
Between the two of us,
who's gonna tell her?

903
01:22:59.292 --> 01:23:00.917
No, surely no one.

904
01:23:01.000 --> 01:23:02.542
Forget "surely."

905
01:23:03.250 --> 01:23:05.292
Forget it, and you'll see
everything turns out fine.

906
01:23:07.167 --> 01:23:08.750
Let him keep working over there,

907
01:23:08.833 --> 01:23:10.792
but he shouldn't think
of taking his daughter.

908
01:23:11.292 --> 01:23:12.958
We'll take good care of her here.

909
01:23:13.917 --> 01:23:14.917
Tell him that, Fulgor.

910
01:23:20.167 --> 01:23:22.750
Once again,
I like how you operate, <i>patrón.</i>

911
01:23:24.125 --> 01:23:26.208
You're getting that youthful spirit back.

912
01:23:48.875 --> 01:23:49.875
Let's go, boys.

913
01:23:50.667 --> 01:23:51.667
Boys.

914
01:23:54.833 --> 01:23:56.458
Welcome, <i>señora.</i>

915
01:23:56.542 --> 01:23:57.667
Please come in.

916
01:23:58.792 --> 01:23:59.792
This way.

917
01:24:06.083 --> 01:24:07.083
Susana.

918
01:24:12.042 --> 01:24:13.625
I'm Pedro Páramo.

919
01:24:14.792 --> 01:24:15.833
Pedro.

920
01:24:27.792 --> 01:24:30.375
<i>Señorita, </i>I'll go with you.

921
01:25:14.208 --> 01:25:15.750
Is that you, Bartolomé?

922
01:25:46.625 --> 01:25:47.625
<i>What have we done?</i>

923
01:25:49.167 --> 01:25:50.792
What's wrong, Damiana?

924
01:25:51.667 --> 01:25:52.833
Why did you scream?

925
01:25:55.125 --> 01:25:56.125
I didn't scream.

926
01:25:57.292 --> 01:25:58.708
You must have been dreaming.

927
01:26:00.542 --> 01:26:02.042
I told you I never dream.

928
01:26:02.875 --> 01:26:03.875
Never.

929
01:26:06.917 --> 01:26:09.583
Besides, I'm exhausted.

930
01:26:11.125 --> 01:26:14.208
You didn't put the cat out last night,
and he wouldn't let me sleep.

931
01:26:15.375 --> 01:26:17.917
The cat slept with me, between my legs.

932
01:26:18.625 --> 01:26:22.208
He was soaked,
so I let him stay in my bed out of pity.

933
01:26:22.917 --> 01:26:25.500
I'm telling you,
he spent the night doing circus tricks.

934
01:26:26.917 --> 01:26:30.208
Even though he is quite affectionate,
I don't want him here while I'm sleeping.

935
01:26:35.583 --> 01:26:37.042
I'm sad for you, Susana.

936
01:26:44.583 --> 01:26:45.917
Your father has died.

937
01:26:48.208 --> 01:26:49.417
He died the night before last,

938
01:26:49.500 --> 01:26:52.292
and today, they told us
that there's nothing to be done.

939
01:26:52.917 --> 01:26:54.292
That they buried him already.

940
01:26:55.917 --> 01:26:58.500
That the journey was too long
for them to bring him here.

941
01:27:03.750 --> 01:27:05.250
You're all alone now.

942
01:27:25.500 --> 01:27:26.708
So then, it was him.

943
01:27:41.292 --> 01:27:43.083
You came to say goodbye.

944
01:28:18.583 --> 01:28:20.042
Tell me what you see, Susana.

945
01:28:21.167 --> 01:28:23.125
I don't see anything, Papa.

946
01:28:24.250 --> 01:28:27.333
I'll lower you some more.
Tell me when you reach the bottom.

947
01:28:31.083 --> 01:28:32.500
Try to find something.

948
01:28:34.458 --> 01:28:35.458
Money!

949
01:28:37.292 --> 01:28:38.875
Round disks of gold.

950
01:28:39.875 --> 01:28:41.000
Look for them, Susana.

951
01:28:57.583 --> 01:28:58.708
Susana!

952
01:29:01.792 --> 01:29:03.083
Susana!

953
01:29:06.000 --> 01:29:07.417
<i>Susana!</i>

954
01:29:11.208 --> 01:29:12.833
<i>Try to find more, Susana!</i>

955
01:29:13.417 --> 01:29:14.583
<i>Money!</i>

956
01:29:26.625 --> 01:29:27.792
Is that you, Father?

957
01:29:29.000 --> 01:29:31.417
I've come to comfort you, my child.

958
01:29:36.000 --> 01:29:38.083
Your heart is dying.

959
01:29:50.958 --> 01:29:53.333
Don't let your heart die out.

960
01:30:08.917 --> 01:30:10.042
Go away, Father.

961
01:30:12.125 --> 01:30:13.292
And don't come back.

962
01:30:16.333 --> 01:30:18.833
Why are you here if you're already dead?

963
01:30:37.708 --> 01:30:39.667
Now open it. There.

964
01:30:40.417 --> 01:30:41.875
Channel the water that way.

965
01:30:43.000 --> 01:30:44.167
Dig deeper.

966
01:30:45.875 --> 01:30:46.875
That way.

967
01:31:04.792 --> 01:31:06.042
I know that one.

968
01:31:07.167 --> 01:31:09.167
He's the foreman over at the Media Luna.

969
01:31:18.333 --> 01:31:19.375
How can I help you?

970
01:31:20.792 --> 01:31:22.417
Do you work for Pedro Páramo?

971
01:31:24.958 --> 01:31:25.792
Yes.

972
01:31:25.875 --> 01:31:28.250
Go tell him we are revolutionaries.

973
01:31:28.792 --> 01:31:30.375
That we've come for his lands.

974
01:31:34.333 --> 01:31:35.583
- All right.
- Run!

975
01:31:36.875 --> 01:31:38.542
Go tell him we'll see him there.

976
01:31:39.417 --> 01:31:40.417
Run faster!

977
01:31:41.542 --> 01:31:42.958
Run faster, man!

978
01:31:43.042 --> 01:31:44.292
Faster!

979
01:32:14.583 --> 01:32:16.458
They didn't pay me no mind.

980
01:32:16.542 --> 01:32:19.792
Poor don Fulgor, he died with one foot up
and the other one down.

981
01:32:20.292 --> 01:32:22.917
Go tell those men
I'm here if they need anything.

982
01:32:23.000 --> 01:32:26.542
They should come deal with me.
What sort of revolutionaries are they?

983
01:32:26.625 --> 01:32:29.292
I don't know.
That's what they called themselves.

984
01:32:30.417 --> 01:32:32.500
But first, swing by La Consagración.

985
01:32:32.583 --> 01:32:34.375
You know El Tilcuate,
the one with one eye?

986
01:32:34.875 --> 01:32:37.333
- Tell him I need him quickly.
- Indeed, <i>patrón.</i>

987
01:33:08.125 --> 01:33:11.208
Gentlemen, what else can I do for you?

988
01:33:11.292 --> 01:33:14.875
Well, as you can see, we've taken up arms.

989
01:33:15.917 --> 01:33:16.917
And?

990
01:33:17.792 --> 01:33:20.292
And that's all.
You don't think that's enough?

991
01:33:21.000 --> 01:33:22.333
I mean, why have you done it?

992
01:33:23.000 --> 01:33:26.042
Because others have done it too.
Haven't you heard?

993
01:33:27.167 --> 01:33:31.792
Just wait for our instructions to come,
and then we'll let you know the cause.

994
01:33:31.875 --> 01:33:33.000
I know the cause.

995
01:33:34.125 --> 01:33:35.708
And if you want, I'll explain it.

996
01:33:39.250 --> 01:33:42.667
We've rebelled against the government
and your kind

997
01:33:42.750 --> 01:33:45.708
because we're tired
of putting up with you.

998
01:33:46.792 --> 01:33:48.625
The government for being scoundrels,

999
01:33:49.583 --> 01:33:54.958
and against you because you're
a bunch of greasy freeloaders and thieves.

1000
01:33:56.042 --> 01:33:58.333
About Mr. Government, we'll say nothing.

1001
01:33:59.458 --> 01:34:02.292
Because we'll tell them
what we want to say with bullets.

1002
01:34:05.417 --> 01:34:07.667
How much do you need for your revolution?

1003
01:34:07.750 --> 01:34:09.500
Perhaps I could help.

1004
01:34:10.000 --> 01:34:12.833
The gentleman here
is making sense, Perseverancio.

1005
01:34:12.917 --> 01:34:16.292
We need a rich friend to help us out.

1006
01:34:16.375 --> 01:34:18.750
And who better than this <i>señor </i>right here?

1007
01:34:19.417 --> 01:34:20.500
Let's see, Casildo!

1008
01:34:21.208 --> 01:34:22.667
How much do we need?

1009
01:34:22.750 --> 01:34:25.417
This guy wouldn't give water
to Saint Peter's rooster.

1010
01:34:27.250 --> 01:34:29.125
Let's make the most of being here now

1011
01:34:30.250 --> 01:34:33.583
and take everything he's got,
down to the corn stuck in his gullet.

1012
01:34:33.667 --> 01:34:36.083
Calm down, Perseverancio.

1013
01:34:36.792 --> 01:34:38.250
Let's come to an agreement.

1014
01:34:39.417 --> 01:34:40.667
You talk, Casildo.

1015
01:34:41.917 --> 01:34:42.917
Um…

1016
01:34:44.000 --> 01:34:50.875
Well, I'd say around 20,000 pesos
would be a good start.

1017
01:34:53.583 --> 01:34:56.292
Or maybe the <i>señor </i>considers
that small change,

1018
01:34:56.375 --> 01:34:59.250
seeing how he's so excited to lend a hand.

1019
01:35:00.708 --> 01:35:02.708
Let's say then, fifty thousand.

1020
01:35:03.958 --> 01:35:04.958
Do you agree?

1021
01:35:11.083 --> 01:35:12.833
I'll give you 100,000 pesos.

1022
01:35:13.333 --> 01:35:14.583
How many are you?

1023
01:35:15.083 --> 01:35:16.250
We're three hundred.

1024
01:35:17.000 --> 01:35:22.083
All right. I'll lend you another 300 men
to grow your contingent.

1025
01:35:22.750 --> 01:35:25.500
You'll have both the men
and the money within the week.

1026
01:35:25.583 --> 01:35:29.167
The money's a gift, the men are on loan.

1027
01:35:33.917 --> 01:35:35.083
I don't see why not.

1028
01:35:35.917 --> 01:35:38.292
Then we'll see you in a week, <i>señores.</i>

1029
01:35:38.375 --> 01:35:40.250
It's been a pleasure to meet you.

1030
01:35:51.542 --> 01:35:53.542
Who do you figure is the one in charge?

1031
01:35:56.167 --> 01:35:59.042
I'd say the one with a big gut
who sat in the middle

1032
01:35:59.125 --> 01:36:00.625
and never once looked up.

1033
01:36:01.583 --> 01:36:02.708
I'd bet it's him.

1034
01:36:02.792 --> 01:36:04.083
No, Damasio.

1035
01:36:04.583 --> 01:36:05.833
You're their boss.

1036
01:36:06.417 --> 01:36:08.375
Or don't you want to join the revolt?

1037
01:36:08.458 --> 01:36:10.500
I can hardly wait.

1038
01:36:10.583 --> 01:36:12.542
Considering how much I like a good rumble.

1039
01:36:12.625 --> 01:36:16.000
You've seen what it's all about,
so you don't need my advice.

1040
01:36:16.083 --> 01:36:19.000
Gather 300 trusty men,
and join up with the rebels.

1041
01:36:19.833 --> 01:36:21.875
You'll figure out the rest on your own.

1042
01:36:22.458 --> 01:36:23.500
What about the money?

1043
01:36:23.583 --> 01:36:25.167
Should I hand it over?

1044
01:36:25.667 --> 01:36:27.500
I'll give you ten pesos for each man.

1045
01:36:27.583 --> 01:36:29.750
Enough for their immediate expenses.

1046
01:36:29.833 --> 01:36:32.667
Tell them I'm keeping the rest safe here
and at their disposal.

1047
01:36:33.958 --> 01:36:35.958
Don't wander too far from my property,

1048
01:36:36.042 --> 01:36:38.375
so if others come,
they'll see the land is occupied.

1049
01:36:38.458 --> 01:36:41.250
And come see me when you can
or when you've got news.

1050
01:36:41.333 --> 01:36:44.292
- It'll be done. See you, <i>patrón.</i>
- Go ahead.

1051
01:36:54.042 --> 01:36:56.417
<i>Now she's the one speaking, Juan Preciado.</i>

1052
01:36:57.625 --> 01:36:58.875
<i>What's she saying?</i>

1053
01:37:00.375 --> 01:37:03.542
<i>She says
that she'd lose herself inside him,</i>

1054
01:37:05.958 --> 01:37:08.292
<i>as she felt her flesh tear open.</i>

1055
01:37:12.000 --> 01:37:14.042
<i>But that his death caused her more pain.</i>

1056
01:37:15.458 --> 01:37:16.625
<i>That's what she's saying.</i>

1057
01:37:17.333 --> 01:37:18.875
<i>Who's she talking about?</i>

1058
01:37:21.458 --> 01:37:24.083
<i>Someone who died before her, surely.</i>

1059
01:38:56.417 --> 01:38:57.625
Margarita.

1060
01:39:02.167 --> 01:39:03.583
Open up, Margarita.

1061
01:40:07.000 --> 01:40:08.875
Little piece of meat.

1062
01:40:19.875 --> 01:40:21.333
It's the sand.

1063
01:40:26.083 --> 01:40:27.667
Bathe with me.

1064
01:40:31.000 --> 01:40:32.250
So much foam…

1065
01:40:35.167 --> 01:40:36.667
When will this be over?

1066
01:40:39.917 --> 01:40:41.458
Nothing can last this long.

1067
01:40:43.583 --> 01:40:47.042
There's no memory,
no matter how intense, that won't fade.

1068
01:40:49.125 --> 01:40:50.667
Maybe it's not a memory.

1069
01:41:12.708 --> 01:41:13.708
Thirty years…

1070
01:41:17.500 --> 01:41:19.083
I waited to have it all.

1071
01:41:20.375 --> 01:41:23.667
Not just something,
but everything that could be had.

1072
01:41:23.750 --> 01:41:24.750
So that…

1073
01:41:26.125 --> 01:41:28.042
there would be nothing left to desire.

1074
01:41:30.042 --> 01:41:31.292
Except you.

1075
01:41:32.708 --> 01:41:33.917
The desire of you.

1076
01:41:42.833 --> 01:41:44.917
When I learned you were finally returning,

1077
01:41:47.250 --> 01:41:49.083
I wanted to embrace you…

1078
01:41:50.292 --> 01:41:51.750
to wrap you in joy.

1079
01:41:54.167 --> 01:41:55.333
And I cried, Susana.

1080
01:41:57.208 --> 01:41:59.333
When I learned you'd finally be returning.

1081
01:42:48.750 --> 01:42:49.875
<i>Señora.</i>

1082
01:43:06.458 --> 01:43:08.792
Isn't it true
that the night is full of sin, Damiana?

1083
01:43:10.500 --> 01:43:11.833
Yes, Susana.

1084
01:43:16.250 --> 01:43:18.500
And what else is life if not sin?

1085
01:43:27.500 --> 01:43:28.542
Don't you hear?

1086
01:43:32.458 --> 01:43:34.292
Don't you hear how the earth grinds?

1087
01:43:38.583 --> 01:43:39.792
No, Susana.

1088
01:43:42.333 --> 01:43:43.417
I don't hear a thing.

1089
01:43:47.333 --> 01:43:49.292
I'm not as fortunate as you.

1090
01:43:51.625 --> 01:43:54.833
You'd be amazed by the things I hear.

1091
01:44:14.500 --> 01:44:16.583
Do you believe in hell, Damiana?

1092
01:44:18.583 --> 01:44:19.583
Yes, Susana.

1093
01:44:21.625 --> 01:44:23.042
And in Heaven as well.

1094
01:44:26.250 --> 01:44:27.958
I only believe in hell.

1095
01:44:45.333 --> 01:44:46.500
How's the <i>señora?</i>

1096
01:44:46.583 --> 01:44:48.333
Bad. Really bad.

1097
01:44:56.583 --> 01:44:57.583
Susana?

1098
01:45:01.542 --> 01:45:03.750
<i>I saw Doña Susanita die.</i>

1099
01:45:05.042 --> 01:45:06.708
<i>What are you saying, Dorotea?</i>

1100
01:45:06.792 --> 01:45:08.375
<i>What I just told you.</i>

1101
01:45:09.917 --> 01:45:12.333
<i>I remember the light
in that window went out,</i>

1102
01:45:12.417 --> 01:45:14.750
<i>after it had been lit
for more than three years.</i>

1103
01:45:15.833 --> 01:45:17.208
<i>Night after night.</i>

1104
01:45:19.250 --> 01:45:21.458
Good. Wait here, then.

1105
01:45:33.292 --> 01:45:35.583
My mouth is filled with soil.

1106
01:45:38.083 --> 01:45:39.292
Yes, Father.

1107
01:45:40.167 --> 01:45:41.792
Don't say, "Yes, Father."

1108
01:45:41.875 --> 01:45:44.208
Repeat what I tell you.

1109
01:45:46.958 --> 01:45:48.500
What are you going to tell me?

1110
01:45:50.250 --> 01:45:52.083
You'll hear my confession again?

1111
01:45:53.042 --> 01:45:56.458
No, Susana.
I've just come to talk with you.

1112
01:45:56.958 --> 01:45:58.708
To prepare you for death.

1113
01:45:59.833 --> 01:46:00.917
Am I going to die?

1114
01:46:03.542 --> 01:46:04.667
Yes, child.

1115
01:46:09.000 --> 01:46:11.208
Then why don't you leave me in peace?

1116
01:46:13.000 --> 01:46:14.667
I want to rest.

1117
01:46:18.083 --> 01:46:19.750
I'll leave you in peace, Susana.

1118
01:46:20.458 --> 01:46:23.625
As you repeat the words I say,

1119
01:46:24.542 --> 01:46:26.292
you'll fall asleep.

1120
01:46:26.792 --> 01:46:29.125
And no one will wake you up.

1121
01:46:30.208 --> 01:46:31.292
All right, Father.

1122
01:46:32.292 --> 01:46:33.583
I'll do as you ask.

1123
01:46:36.375 --> 01:46:39.583
My mouth is filled with soil.

1124
01:46:45.208 --> 01:46:47.958
<i>I swallow the foam of my saliva.</i>

1125
01:46:48.958 --> 01:46:53.833
<i>I chew clumps of soil,
crawling with worms.</i>

1126
01:46:56.375 --> 01:47:01.500
My mouth twists out of shape,
pierced by teeth.

1127
01:47:03.250 --> 01:47:07.625
<i>The gelatin of my eyes melts.</i>

1128
01:47:08.333 --> 01:47:11.750
<i>The hair burns in one lone blaze…</i>

1129
01:47:17.208 --> 01:47:19.375
He sheltered me in his arms.

1130
01:47:21.583 --> 01:47:22.833
He gave me love.

1131
01:47:25.792 --> 01:47:27.292
There's more.

1132
01:47:29.083 --> 01:47:30.625
The sight of God.

1133
01:47:31.792 --> 01:47:37.292
The last fleeting image seen
by those condemned to eternal suffering.

1134
01:47:38.917 --> 01:47:41.833
<i>The gentle light of His infinite Heaven.</i>

1135
01:47:41.917 --> 01:47:44.417
<i>The joy of the cherubim.</i>

1136
01:47:45.000 --> 01:47:47.458
God's joyful gaze.

1137
01:47:49.125 --> 01:47:50.667
And not only that,

1138
01:47:51.875 --> 01:47:57.167
all of it coalesced
with profound earthly sorrow.

1139
01:48:04.750 --> 01:48:08.708
The marrow of our bones set ablaze.

1140
01:48:10.708 --> 01:48:14.542
<i>The blood in our veins
turns to strings of fire.</i>

1141
01:48:15.625 --> 01:48:19.958
<i>Forcing us to wallow in an immense pain…</i>

1142
01:48:21.875 --> 01:48:23.667
<i>that never recedes…</i>

1143
01:48:24.958 --> 01:48:28.542
<i>stoked by the wrath of the Lord.</i>

1144
01:48:40.000 --> 01:48:42.208
You'll appear before God.

1145
01:48:43.417 --> 01:48:46.667
And His judgment of sinners is inhumane.

1146
01:48:53.583 --> 01:48:55.083
Go now, Father.

1147
01:48:57.125 --> 01:48:58.750
Don't fret over me.

1148
01:49:00.625 --> 01:49:02.042
I'm at peace.

1149
01:49:03.792 --> 01:49:05.542
And I want to sleep.

1150
01:49:15.583 --> 01:49:16.583
Damiana.

1151
01:49:17.458 --> 01:49:19.375
Please go cry somewhere else.

1152
01:51:24.333 --> 01:51:27.333
<i>The tolling for that death
lasted longer than it should have.</i>

1153
01:51:33.167 --> 01:51:35.792
<i>People began arriving from all over,</i>

1154
01:51:35.875 --> 01:51:38.417
<i>drawn in by the ringing of the bells.</i>

1155
01:51:53.917 --> 01:51:57.625
<i>And little by little,
things turned into a big party.</i>

1156
01:51:58.708 --> 01:52:03.708
<i>Comala was teeming with people,
with celebrations, and noise.</i>

1157
01:52:06.583 --> 01:52:08.958
Hey! She's in the air!

1158
01:52:10.125 --> 01:52:12.208
Amazing!

1159
01:52:14.750 --> 01:52:16.042
Don't get in the way!

1160
01:52:32.750 --> 01:52:34.750
<i>The bells finally stopped ringing…</i>

1161
01:52:35.875 --> 01:52:37.500
<i>…but the party continued.</i>

1162
01:52:38.875 --> 01:52:41.167
<i>There was no way to make them understand</i>

1163
01:52:41.250 --> 01:52:45.042
<i>it was mourning, days of mourning.</i>

1164
01:54:20.542 --> 01:54:21.542
Fire!

1165
01:54:49.042 --> 01:54:51.208
Don't keep standing there, Don Pedro.

1166
01:54:53.542 --> 01:54:54.792
Sit down, at least.

1167
01:54:56.625 --> 01:54:58.000
I'll cross my arms,

1168
01:54:59.208 --> 01:55:01.417
and Comala will die of hunger.

1169
01:56:15.708 --> 01:56:16.708
<i>Patrón.</i>

1170
01:56:19.250 --> 01:56:21.667
Father Rentería has taken up arms.

1171
01:56:22.917 --> 01:56:24.333
And why is that?

1172
01:56:25.167 --> 01:56:29.542
Because the revolutionary government
has suspended holy services.

1173
01:56:32.458 --> 01:56:34.458
Weren't you with Villa?

1174
01:56:35.292 --> 01:56:37.208
Or was it Obregón?

1175
01:56:39.083 --> 01:56:41.208
Peace has been made there, Don Pedro.

1176
01:56:42.208 --> 01:56:43.458
We're on our own.

1177
01:56:45.500 --> 01:56:46.500
What should we do?

1178
01:56:47.500 --> 01:56:49.208
Join him or fight him?

1179
01:56:50.250 --> 01:56:51.792
No question about it.

1180
01:56:52.583 --> 01:56:54.250
Take the side of the government.

1181
01:56:54.333 --> 01:56:56.167
But we're irregulars.

1182
01:56:57.208 --> 01:56:58.792
They consider us rebels.

1183
01:57:00.708 --> 01:57:02.458
Do what you want, then.

1184
01:57:03.292 --> 01:57:05.292
I'll join up with the priest.

1185
01:57:05.875 --> 01:57:07.333
I like how he yells.

1186
01:57:08.167 --> 01:57:10.833
Besides, fighting on his side,
salvation is guaranteed.

1187
01:57:18.125 --> 01:57:19.292
Well, <i>patrón…</i>

1188
01:57:21.083 --> 01:57:22.208
I'll see you.

1189
01:57:44.458 --> 01:57:46.417
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

1190
01:58:18.125 --> 01:58:22.333
<i>Since Pedro Páramo threw the people out</i>
<i>and sat down on his </i>equipal <i>chair…</i>

1191
01:58:24.042 --> 01:58:26.500
<i>the land became a wasteland
and was left in ruins.</i>

1192
01:58:29.625 --> 01:58:31.792
<i>The town started emptying.</i>

1193
01:58:32.792 --> 01:58:35.250
<i>All around, people wasted away.</i>

1194
01:58:36.500 --> 01:58:38.750
<i>And Comala filled with farewells.</i>

1195
01:58:41.375 --> 01:58:43.750
<i>I stayed because I had nowhere to go.</i>

1196
01:58:45.833 --> 01:58:49.208
<i>But with the people, the charity
that kept me alive also left.</i>

1197
01:58:50.875 --> 01:58:52.667
<i>And I started starving to death.</i>

1198
01:58:55.167 --> 01:58:57.292
<i>After we found you,</i>

1199
01:58:57.375 --> 01:58:59.875
<i>my bones were determined
to find some rest.</i>

1200
01:59:01.125 --> 01:59:02.375
<i>What about your soul?</i>

1201
01:59:03.917 --> 01:59:05.417
<i>Where do you think it went?</i>

1202
01:59:07.667 --> 01:59:11.625
<i>It begged me to get back up
and carry on with my life.</i>

1203
01:59:12.333 --> 01:59:16.250
<i>As if it hoped for some miracle
to cleanse my sins.</i>

1204
01:59:17.708 --> 01:59:19.625
<i>I didn't even try.</i>

1205
01:59:22.292 --> 01:59:24.417
<i>I opened my mouth to let it escape.</i>

1206
01:59:26.042 --> 01:59:27.208
<i>And it took off.</i>

1207
01:59:29.708 --> 01:59:33.583
<i>I felt when the thread of blood
that joined it to my heart</i>

1208
01:59:33.667 --> 01:59:34.875
<i>fell onto my hands.</i>

1209
01:59:39.667 --> 01:59:41.542
<i>I thought no one would mind me.</i>

1210
01:59:44.792 --> 01:59:47.208
<i>I never get in anybody's way.</i>

1211
01:59:50.542 --> 01:59:53.250
<i>I didn't even need my own space
here in the ground.</i>

1212
01:59:54.917 --> 01:59:57.042
<i>They buried me in your grave,</i>

1213
01:59:57.125 --> 02:00:00.167
<i>tucked away in the hollow of your arms.</i>

1214
02:00:02.125 --> 02:00:06.542
<i>It occurred to me, I should be the one
holding you in my arms.</i>

1215
02:00:32.500 --> 02:00:33.708
<i>What about Pedro Páramo?</i>

1216
02:00:35.708 --> 02:00:39.708
<i>Years passed, and he was always there,
like a scarecrow.</i>

1217
02:00:40.958 --> 02:00:43.708
<i>He'd forgotten about sleep and time.</i>

1218
02:00:44.667 --> 02:00:48.625
<i>Because he was afraid of the nights
that filled the darkness with ghosts.</i>

1219
02:00:50.125 --> 02:00:52.458
<i>To be locked up with his ghosts.</i>

1220
02:00:53.292 --> 02:00:54.750
<i>That's what he was scared of.</i>

1221
02:00:55.458 --> 02:00:56.542
Damiana!

1222
02:00:58.333 --> 02:01:00.042
Come and see what this man wants.

1223
02:01:29.000 --> 02:01:32.083
Give me some money to bury my wife.

1224
02:01:33.500 --> 02:01:37.167
Deliver us, O Lord,
from the snares of the evil one.

1225
02:01:39.042 --> 02:01:40.250
What did you say?

1226
02:01:47.792 --> 02:01:51.750
I've come for a little something
to bury my wife.

1227
02:01:52.250 --> 02:01:55.792
I was forced to sell my mules
to pay the doctor, but…

1228
02:01:55.875 --> 02:01:57.583
Just go.

1229
02:01:57.667 --> 02:01:59.583
It was all for nothing, you know?

1230
02:02:02.958 --> 02:02:03.958
She's there…

1231
02:02:05.917 --> 02:02:07.083
alone…

1232
02:02:08.583 --> 02:02:10.417
enduring the damp air.

1233
02:02:14.125 --> 02:02:15.208
Help!

1234
02:02:15.292 --> 02:02:18.333
Help! Somebody help us!

1235
02:02:24.250 --> 02:02:25.500
Give me something.

1236
02:02:32.375 --> 02:02:33.458
Give me something!

1237
02:02:36.125 --> 02:02:37.500
Give me something!

1238
02:02:58.333 --> 02:02:59.625
Are you all right, <i>patrón?</i>

1239
02:03:17.708 --> 02:03:18.708
Let's go.

1240
02:03:53.875 --> 02:03:55.083
It's me, Don Pedro.

1241
02:03:57.958 --> 02:03:59.917
Would you like me
to bring out your lunch?

1242
02:04:01.667 --> 02:04:02.708
I'm coming.

1243
02:04:07.958 --> 02:04:09.000
I'm coming now.

1244
02:04:52.917 --> 02:04:57.375
BASED ON THE NOVEL BY JUAN RULFO

1245
02:10:30.083 --> 02:10:32.083
Adapted subtitles by Leon Elalouf
